{"timestamp": "2026-07-28T14:32:53.717759", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "no_mem", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_42576abe-0deb-4869-8c63-225c2d75a95a", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: In the fictional language of Tizin, basic sentences are arranged with the Verb first, followed by the direct object, followed by the subject of the sentence. I want to express my love for apples to my Tizin friend. \n\nThe word that indicates oneself is \"Pa\" is the nominative form, \"Mato\" is the accusative form, and \"Sing\" is the genitive form. \n\nThe root verb that indicates an intense like for something is \"Maktay\". When it is used in the prese", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "Maktay Mato Apple", "expected": "Maktay mato apple", "score": 1.0, "em": 1.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "1", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 0, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": null, "fb_mode": "gold", "code_rev": "3f7502f7.ff40ae22", "critic_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "gold", "judge_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "protocol_hash": "c6b1ff544be8", "prof_total_s": 37.68, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 37.68, "prof_tok_in": 469, "prof_tok_out": 2175, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
