{"timestamp": "2026-07-28T14:33:15.193330", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "no_mem", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_708b99c5-e4a7-49cb-a5cf-933c8d46470d", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: On the DeepFruits fruit detection graph on Connected Papers from 2016, what feature caused the largest bubble to be the size it is?", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "Connected Papers represents each paper as a node (bubble) in a similarity graph. According to the platform's design, the size of each bubble is scaled according to the paper's total citation count (the number of times it has been cited in the literature). On the DeepFruits (2016) fruit detection graph, the largest bubble corresponds to the most highly cited paper in that network (e.g., a foundational deep learning or object detection paper), and its size is solely a function of its exceptionally high citation count rather than its age, authorship, or position in the graph.\n\nThe number of citations (citation count) the paper has received", "expected": "Citations", "score": 1.0, "em": 1.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "2", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 0, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": null, "fb_mode": "gold", "code_rev": "3f7502f7.ff40ae22", "critic_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "gold", "judge_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "protocol_hash": "c6b1ff544be8", "prof_total_s": 59.15, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 59.15, "prof_tok_in": 537, "prof_tok_out": 3152, "prof_llm_calls": 2}
