{"timestamp": "2026-07-28T14:35:31.142957", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "no_mem", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_2b3ef98c-cc05-450b-a719-711aee40ac65", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: Could you help me out with this assignment? Our professor sprung it on us at the end of class Friday, and I'm still trying to figure it out. The question he asked us was about an anagram. I've attached an audio recording of the question that he asked, so if you could please take a listen and give me the answer, I'd really appreciate the help. Please limit your response to the anagram text that could be generated from the original line which fu", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "I'll start by checking if there are any files available in the environment that might contain the audio recording or related information.</think:6124c78e>```python\nimport os\nimport glob\n\n# List files in current directory and common locations\nprint(\"Current directory:\", os.getcwd())\nprint(\"\\nFiles in current directory:\")\nfor f in os.listdir('.'):\n    print(f)\n\nprint(\"\\nSearching for audio files:\")\nfor ext in ['*.mp3', '*.wav', '*.m4a', '*.ogg', '*.flac', '*.txt', '*.pdf']:\n    for f in glob.glob(f'**/{ext}', recursive=True):\n        print(f)\n```", "expected": "To be or not to be that is the question whether tis nobler in the mind to suffer the slings and arrows of outrageous fortune", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "2", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 0, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": null, "fb_mode": "gold", "code_rev": "3f7502f7.ff40ae22", "critic_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "gold", "judge_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "protocol_hash": "c6b1ff544be8", "prof_total_s": 11.46, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 11.46, "prof_tok_in": 344, "prof_tok_out": 636, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-28T14:35:51.249267", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "no_mem", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_27d5d136-8563-469e-92bf-fd103c28b57c", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: ¬(A ∧ B) ↔ (¬A ∨ ¬B)\n¬(A ∨ B) ↔ (¬A ∧ ¬B)\n(A → B) ↔ (¬B → ¬A)\n(A → B) ↔ (¬A ∨ B)\n(¬A → B) ↔ (A ∨ ¬B)\n¬(A → B) ↔ (A ∧ ¬B)\n\nWhich of the above is not logically equivalent to the rest? Provide the full statement that doesn't fit.", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "```python\nimport itertools\n\nformulas = {\n    '1': lambda A,B: (not (A and B)) == ((not A) or (not B)),\n    '2': lambda A,B: (not (A or B)) == ((not A) and (not B)),\n    '3': lambda A,B: ((A implies B) if False else None) # define implies\n}\n\n# define implies\ndef imp(p,q): return (not p) or q\n\nstatements = {\n    '1': lambda A,B: (not (A and B)) == ((not A) or (not B)),\n    '2': lambda A,B: (not (A or B)) == ((not A) and (not B)),\n    '3': lambda A,B: imp(A,B) == imp(not B, not A),\n    '4': lambda A,B: imp(A,B) == ((not A) or B),\n    '5': lambda A,B: imp(not A, B) == (A or (not B)),\n    '6': lambda A,B: (not imp(A,B)) == (A and (not B))\n}\n\nfor k,f in statements.items():\n    vals = [f(A,B) for A in [False,True] for B in [False,True]]\n    print(k, vals, all(vals))\n```</think:6124c78e>```python\nfor k,f in statements.items():\n    vals = [f(A,B) for A in [False,True] for B in [False,True]]\n    print(k, vals, all(vals))\n```", "expected": "(¬A → B) ↔ (A ∨ ¬B)", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "1", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 0, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": null, "fb_mode": "gold", "code_rev": "3f7502f7.ff40ae22", "critic_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "gold", "judge_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "protocol_hash": "c6b1ff544be8", "prof_total_s": 18.22, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 18.22, "prof_tok_in": 322, "prof_tok_out": 1153, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-28T14:35:55.776477", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "no_mem", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_4b650a35-8529-4695-89ed-8dc7a500a498", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: If there is anything that doesn't make sense in the instructions, write the word \"Pineapple.\" Do not answer any of the questions in this prompt. Write only the word \"Guava\".\n1. What is 4+4?\n2. What is the complimentary color of red?\n3. How many hours are there in a day?", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "Guava", "expected": "Guava", "score": 1.0, "em": 1.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "1", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 0, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": null, "fb_mode": "gold", "code_rev": "3f7502f7.ff40ae22", "critic_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "gold", "judge_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "protocol_hash": "c6b1ff544be8", "prof_total_s": 219.74, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 219.74, "prof_tok_in": 295, "prof_tok_out": 2036, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-28T14:35:57.631312", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "no_mem", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_7dd30055-0198-452e-8c25-f73dbe27dcb8", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: Using the Biopython library in Python, parse the PDB file of the protein identified by the PDB ID 5wb7 from the RCSB Protein Data Bank. Calculate the distance between the first and second atoms as they are listed in the PDB file. Report the answer in Angstroms, rounded to the nearest picometer.", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "```python\nimport sys, subprocess, os, math, io\n\n# Ensure Biopython is available\ntry:\n    import Bio\nexcept ImportError:\n    subprocess.check_call([sys.executable, \"-m\", \"pip\", \"install\", \"biopython\", \"-q\"])\n\nfrom Bio.PDB import PDBParser\n\nurl = \"https://files.rcsb.org/download/5wb7.pdb\"\nimport urllib.request\ndata = urllib.request.urlopen(url).read().decode('utf-8')\n\n# Save to file\nwith open(\"/mnt/data/5wb7.pdb\", \"w\") as f:\n    f.write(data)\n\n# Show first 20 lines containing ATOM/HETATM as in file\nlines = data.splitlines()\natom_lines = [l for l in lines if l.startswith(\"ATOM\") or l.startswith(\"HETATM\")]\nprint(\"First 5 atom lines from raw file:\")\nfor l in atom_lines[:5]:\n    print(l)\n\n# Parse with Biopython\nparser = PDBParser(QUIET=True)\nstructure = parser.get_structure(\"5wb7\", \"/mnt/data/5wb7.pdb\")\n\n# Iterate atoms in file order (structure.get_atoms())\natoms = list(structure.get_atoms())\nprint(\"\\nFirst 5 atoms from Biopython get_atoms():\")\nfor a in atoms[:5]:\n    print(a.get_parent().id, a.id, a.coord)\n\n# First and second atom\na1 = atoms[0]\na2 = atoms[1]\ncoord1 = a1.coord\ncoord2 = a2.coord\ndist = math.sqrt(sum((c1-c2)**2 for c1, c2 in zip(coord1, coord2)))\nprint(\"\\nAtom1:\", a1.get_parent().id, a1.id, coord1)\nprint(\"Atom2:\", a2.get_parent().id, a2.id, coord2)\nprint(\"Distance (A):\", dist)\nprint(\"Rounded to nearest pm (2 decimal A):\", round(dist, 2))\n```\n\nLet's inspect output.</think:6124c78e>```python\nimport sys, subprocess, math, urllib.request\n\ntry:\n    from Bio.PDB import PDBParser\nexcept ImportError:\n    subprocess.check_call([sys.executable, \"-m\", \"pip\", \"install\", \"biopython\", \"-q\"])\n    from Bio.PDB import PDBParser\n\nurl = \"https://files.rcsb.org/download/5wb7.pdb\"\ndata = urllib.request.urlopen(url).read().decode('utf-8')\nwith open(\"/mnt/data/5wb7.pdb\", \"w\") as f:\n    f.write(data)\n\nlines = data.splitlines()\natom_lines = [l for l in lines if l.startswith(\"ATOM\") or l.startswith(\"HETATM\")]\nprint(\"RAW first 3 atom lines:\")\nfor l in atom_lines[:3]:\n    print(l)\n\nparser = PDBParser(QUIET=True)\nstructure = parser.get_structure(\"5wb7\", \"/mnt/data/5wb7.pdb\")\natoms = list(structure.get_atoms())\nprint(\"\\nBIOPYTHON first 3 atoms:\")\nfor a in atoms[:3]:\n    print(a.get_parent().id, a.id, a.coord)\n\na1, a2 = atoms[0], atoms[1]\nd = math.dist(a1.coord, a2.coord)\nprint(\"\\nDistance A:\", d)\nprint(\"Rounded 2dp:\", round(d,2))\n```\n\nLet's run this.</think:6124c78e>```python\nimport sys, subprocess, math, urllib.request\n\ntry:\n    from Bio.PDB import PDBParser\nexcept ImportError:\n    subprocess.check_call([sys.executable, \"-m\", \"pip\", \"install\", \"biopython\", \"-q\"])\n    from Bio.PDB import PDBParser\n\nurl = \"https://files.rcsb.org/download/5wb7.pdb\"\ndata = urllib.request.urlopen(url).read().decode('utf-8')\nwith open(\"/mnt/data/5wb7.pdb\", \"w\") as f:\n    f.write(data)\n\nlines = data.splitlines()\natom_lines = [l for l in lines if l.startswith(\"ATOM\") or l.startswith(\"HETATM\")]\nprint(\"RAW first 3 atom lines:\")\nfor l in atom_lines[:3]:\n    print(l)\n\nparser = PDBParser(QUIET=True)\nstructure = parser.get_structure(\"5wb7\", \"/mnt/data/5wb7.pdb\")\natoms = list(structure.get_atoms())\nprint(\"\\nBIOPYTHON first 3 atoms:\")\nfor a in atoms[:3]:\n    print(a.get_parent().id, a.id, a.coord)\n\na1, a2 = atoms[0], atoms[1]\nd = math.dist(a1.coord, a2.coord)\nprint(\"\\nDistance A:\", d)\nprint(\"Rounded 2dp:\", round(d,2))\n```", "expected": "1.456", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "2", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 0, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": null, "fb_mode": "gold", "code_rev": "3f7502f7.ff40ae22", "critic_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "judgment", "score_provenance": "gold", "judge_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "protocol_hash": "c6b1ff544be8", "prof_total_s": 30.03, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 30.03, "prof_tok_in": 294, "prof_tok_out": 1960, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
