{"timestamp": "2026-07-28T14:38:55.883752", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "no_mem", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_54612da3-fd56-4941-80f4-5eb82330de25", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: The attached file shows the locomotives in the collection of a North American railroad museum. How many wheels do the listed steam locomotives have in total?", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "Since no file is attached in this environment and I have no tools to read external files, I cannot access the list of locomotives or their wheel counts. Therefore, the total number of wheels for the listed steam locomotives cannot be calculated from the information provided.\n\nUnable to determine (no file provided)", "expected": "60", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "2", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 0, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": null, "fb_mode": "gold", "code_rev": "3f7502f7.ff40ae22", "critic_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "guarded", "score_provenance": "gold", "judge_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "protocol_hash": "cda8cfafe9da", "prof_total_s": 49.71, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 49.71, "prof_tok_in": 535, "prof_tok_out": 3095, "prof_llm_calls": 2}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-28T14:39:07.896318", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "no_mem", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_a7feb290-76bb-4cb7-8800-7edaf7954f2f", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: How many High Energy Physics - Lattice articles listed in January 2020 on Arxiv had ps versions available?", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "arXiv deprecated PostScript (PS) generation for new submissions starting in 2018, so any articles listed in the hep-lat category in January 2020 would not have PS versions available.\n\n0", "expected": "31", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "2", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 0, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": null, "fb_mode": "gold", "code_rev": "3f7502f7.ff40ae22", "critic_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "guarded", "score_provenance": "gold", "judge_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "protocol_hash": "cda8cfafe9da", "prof_total_s": 49.73, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 49.73, "prof_tok_in": 525, "prof_tok_out": 2700, "prof_llm_calls": 2}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-28T14:39:14.332008", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "no_mem", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_851e570a-e3de-4d84-bcfa-cc85578baa59", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: I thought we could try a fun word puzzle together :)\n\nI've got a Boggle board here:\n\nABRL\nEITE\nIONS\nFPEI\n\nI'd like to know the longest word that can be generated from the board. Please find the longest English language word that can be generated from this board. If more than one word of the same length exists at the maximum word length, please report the longest word that comes first, alphabetically. Oh, and I know that there might be differen", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "```python\nimport urllib.request, sys, time\n\nurl = \"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/dwyl/english-words/master/words_alpha.txt\"\nprint(\"Downloading dictionary...\")\ndata = urllib.request.urlopen(url).read().decode('utf-8')\nwords = [w.strip().lower() for w in data.splitlines() if w.strip()]\nprint(\"Dictionary size:\", len(words))\n\nboard = [\n    ['a','b','r','l'],\n    ['e','i','t','e'],\n    ['i','o','n','s'],\n    ['f','p','e','i']\n]\n\n# Build trie\nclass TrieNode:\n    __slots__ = ('children', 'is_word')\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.children = {}\n        self.is_word = False\n\nroot = TrieNode()\nfor w in words:\n    node = root\n    for ch in w:\n        if ch not in node.children:\n            node.children[ch] = TrieNode()\n        node = node.children[ch]\n    node.is_word = True\n\n# Boggle search\nrows = 4\ncols = 4\nfound = set()\n\ndef dfs(r, c, node, path, visited):\n    ch = board[r][c]\n    if ch not in node.children:\n        return\n    node = node.children[ch]\n    path.append(ch)\n    visited.add((r,c))\n    if node.is_word and len(path) >= 3:  # standard boggle min length 3, but we only care longest\n        found.add(''.join(path))\n    # explore neighbors\n    for dr in (-1,0,1):\n        for dc in (-1,0,1):\n            if dr==0 and dc==0: continue\n            nr, nc = r+dr, c+dc\n            if 0 <= nr < rows and 0 <= nc < cols and (nr,nc) not in visited:\n                dfs(nr, nc, node, path, visited)\n    path.pop()\n    visited.remove((r,c))\n\nfor r in range(rows):\n    for c in range(cols):\n        dfs(r, c, root, [], set())\n\nprint(\"Total words found:\", len(found))\nif found:\n    max_len = max(len(w) for w in found)\n    longest = sorted([w for w in found if len(w)==max_len])\n    print(\"Max length:\", max_len)\n    print(\"Longest words (alpha first):\", longest[:10])\n    print(\"Answer:\", longest[0])\nelse:\n    print(\"No words found\")\n```", "expected": "Briniest", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "3", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 0, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": null, "fb_mode": "gold", "code_rev": "3f7502f7.ff40ae22", "critic_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "guarded", "score_provenance": "gold", "judge_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "protocol_hash": "cda8cfafe9da", "prof_total_s": 50.41, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 50.41, "prof_tok_in": 362, "prof_tok_out": 1298, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
