{"timestamp": "2026-07-28T14:40:00.905799", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "no_mem", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_5cfb274c-0207-4aa7-9575-6ac0bd95d9b2", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: Each cell in the attached spreadsheet represents a plot of land. The color of the cell indicates who owns that plot. Green cells are plots owned by Earl Smith. Can Earl walk through every plot he owns (and no other plots) and return to his starting plot without backtracking? For this question, consider backtracking to be any instance where Earl would enter a plot of land he had already entered since leaving his starting plot.", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "The question refers to an \"attached spreadsheet\" that defines a grid of land plots and identifies Earl Smith's plots as green cells. To determine whether Earl can walk through every green plot exactly once and return to his start without re-entering any plot (i.e., whether the subgraph of green cells contains a Hamiltonian cycle), we must know the specific layout, adjacency, and connectivity of those green cells. No spreadsheet, grid, or description of cell colors has been provided in this environment. Therefore, the required spatial information is missing and the query cannot be evaluated.\n\nCannot be determined (spreadsheet not provided)", "expected": "No", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "1", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 0, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": null, "fb_mode": "gold", "code_rev": "3f7502f7.ff40ae22", "critic_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "guarded", "score_provenance": "gold", "judge_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "protocol_hash": "cda8cfafe9da", "prof_total_s": 103.28, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 103.28, "prof_tok_in": 649, "prof_tok_out": 4871, "prof_llm_calls": 2}
