{"timestamp": "2026-07-28T14:45:00.882751", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "no_mem", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_3ff6b7a9-a5bd-4412-ad92-0cd0d45c0fee", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: The longest-lived vertebrate is named after an island.  According to Wikipedia as of January 1, 2021, what is the 2020 estimated population of that island, to the nearest thousand?", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "The longest-lived vertebrate is the Greenland shark, named after Greenland. Wikipedia’s 2020 population estimate for Greenland was 56,081, which rounds to the nearest thousand as 56,000.\n\n56,000", "expected": "56000", "score": 1.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "2", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 0, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": null, "fb_mode": "gold", "code_rev": "3f7502f7.ff40ae22", "critic_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "guarded", "score_provenance": "gold", "judge_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "protocol_hash": "cda8cfafe9da", "prof_total_s": 366.72, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 366.72, "prof_tok_in": 561, "prof_tok_out": 2446, "prof_llm_calls": 2}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-28T14:45:17.501880", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "no_mem", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_56db2318-640f-477a-a82f-bc93ad13e882", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: The following numbers function similarly to ISBN 13 numbers, however, their validation methods are slightly different. Rather than using alternate weights of 1 and 3, the checksum digit is calculated with an alternate weight of 1 and some other positive integer less than 10. Otherwise, the checksum digit is calculated as expected. Unfortunately, there is an error in the data. Two adjacent columns have been transposed. These errored columns do ", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "```python\nimport itertools\n\nnumbers = [\n    \"9783541813919\",\n    \"9789466697461\",\n    \"9783980361396\",\n    \"9784476566804\",\n    \"9782795866647\",\n    \"9785950736933\",\n    \"9789766476526\",\n    \"9785911781255\",\n    \"9787284659245\",\n    \"9784148251559\",\n]\n\ndef valid_with_swap(w, y):\n    # weights: index i -> 1 if i%2==0 else w\n    for s in numbers:\n        # swap columns y and y+1\n        lst = list(s)\n        lst[y], lst[y+1] = lst[y+1], lst[y]\n        digits = [int(c) for c in lst]\n        total = sum(d * (1 if i%2==0 else w) for i,d in enumerate(digits))\n        if total % 10 != 0:\n            return False\n    return True\n\nsolutions = []\nfor w in range(2,10):\n    for y in range(3,11):  # y+1 <=11 => y<=10\n        if valid_with_swap(w,y):\n            solutions.append((w,y))\nsolutions\n```", "expected": "7, 9", "score": 1.0, "em": 1.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "3", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": null, "fb_mode": "gold", "code_rev": "3f7502f7.ff40ae22", "critic_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "guarded", "score_provenance": "gold", "judge_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "protocol_hash": "cda8cfafe9da", "prof_total_s": 478.44, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 478.44, "prof_tok_in": 469, "prof_tok_out": 1946, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
