{"timestamp": "2026-07-28T14:49:19.045495", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "no_mem", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_3cef3a44-215e-4aed-8e3b-b1e3f08063b7", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: I'm making a grocery list for my mom, but she's a professor of botany and she's a real stickler when it comes to categorizing things. I need to add different foods to different categories on the grocery list, but if I make a mistake, she won't buy anything inserted in the wrong category. Here's the list I have so far:\n\nmilk, eggs, flour, whole bean coffee, Oreos, sweet potatoes, fresh basil, plums, green beans, rice, corn, bell pepper, whole a", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "To classify these items botanically for a stickler botany professor, we must separate true vegetables (edible roots, stems, leaves, flowers) from botanical fruits (developed from the ovary, containing seeds) and other non-vegetable items. \n\n- Milk, eggs, flour, Oreos: animal/processed, not plants.\n- Whole bean coffee, rice, peanuts: seeds/grains (not vegetables).\n- Plums, green beans, corn, bell pepper, whole allspice, acorns, zucchini: botanical fruits (legumes, berries, drupes, grains, nuts are fruits).\n- Sweet potatoes: storage roots → vegetable.\n- Fresh basil: leaves → vegetable.\n- Broccoli: flower buds/stems → vegetable.\n- Celery: petioles (stems) → vegetable.\n- Lettuce: leaves → vegetable.\n\nAlphabetizing the vegetables from the original list items yields: broccoli, celery, fresh basil, lettuce, sweet potatoes.\n\nbroccoli, celery, fresh basil, lettuce, sweet potatoes", "expected": "broccoli, celery, fresh basil, lettuce, sweet potatoes", "score": 1.0, "em": 1.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "1", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": null, "fb_mode": "gold", "code_rev": "3f7502f7.ff40ae22", "critic_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "guarded", "score_provenance": "gold", "judge_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "protocol_hash": "cda8cfafe9da", "prof_total_s": 503.17, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 503.17, "prof_tok_in": 941, "prof_tok_out": 5750, "prof_llm_calls": 2}
