{"timestamp": "2026-07-28T14:51:23.034594", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "no_mem", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_7d4a7d1d-cac6-44a8-96e8-ea9584a70825", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: According to Girls Who Code, how long did it take in years for the percentage of computer scientists that were women to change by 13% from a starting point of 37%?", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "Girls Who Code cites that in 1995, 37% of computer scientists were women, and that this figure fell to 24% — a 13-percentage-point drop. They attribute this decline to having occurred over a 20-year period (from 1995 to around 2015).\n\n20 years", "expected": "22", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "1", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": null, "fb_mode": "gold", "code_rev": "3f7502f7.ff40ae22", "critic_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "guarded", "score_provenance": "gold", "judge_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "protocol_hash": "cda8cfafe9da", "prof_total_s": 474.97, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 474.97, "prof_tok_in": 553, "prof_tok_out": 2278, "prof_llm_calls": 2}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-28T14:51:35.967242", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "no_mem", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_4d51c4bf-4b0e-4f3d-897b-3f6687a7d9f2", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: This spreadsheet contains a list of clients for a retractable awning company. Each client has ordered a new awning for the back of their house within the last 90 days. The company makes different designs depending on whether the awning is made to block sunrises or sunsets. In this region, houses with odd-numbered street addresses face east, and houses with even-numbered street addresses face west. How many of these clients will be receiving th", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "The question requires identifying clients with even-numbered street addresses (west-facing houses that need sunset-blocking awnings). However, the spreadsheet or client list referenced in the prompt was not actually provided, and no tools are available to retrieve it. Therefore, the count cannot be computed from the information given.\n\nUnable to determine (spreadsheet data not provided)", "expected": "8", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "2", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": null, "fb_mode": "gold", "code_rev": "3f7502f7.ff40ae22", "critic_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "guarded", "score_provenance": "gold", "judge_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "protocol_hash": "cda8cfafe9da", "prof_total_s": 441.66, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 441.66, "prof_tok_in": 673, "prof_tok_out": 2295, "prof_llm_calls": 2}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-28T14:51:53.284463", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "no_mem", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_8d46b8d6-b38a-47ff-ac74-cda14cf2d19b", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: What percentage of the total penguin population according to the upper estimates on english Wikipedia at the end of 2012 is made up by the penguins in this file that don't live on Dream Island or have beaks longer than 42mm? Round to the nearest five decimal places.", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "The upper estimate for the total penguin population on English Wikipedia at the end of 2012 was 20,000,000 (breeding pairs treated as the population figure). In the standard penguins dataset (344 rows), the penguins that fail the condition (i.e., live on Dream Island and have bill length ≤ 42 mm) number 50, so the qualifying penguins are 344 − 50 = 294. The percentage is (294 / 20,000,000) × 100 = 0.00147%.\n\n0.00147", "expected": "0.00033", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "3", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 0, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": null, "fb_mode": "gold", "code_rev": "3f7502f7.ff40ae22", "critic_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "guarded", "score_provenance": "gold", "judge_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "protocol_hash": "cda8cfafe9da", "prof_total_s": 723.63, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 723.63, "prof_tok_in": 591, "prof_tok_out": 29196, "prof_llm_calls": 2}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-28T14:51:54.976286", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "no_mem", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_a7feb290-76bb-4cb7-8800-7edaf7954f2f", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: How many High Energy Physics - Lattice articles listed in January 2020 on Arxiv had ps versions available?", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "arXiv discontinued generating PostScript (PS) files for new submissions starting in January 2018, and the January 2020 listing for the High Energy Physics - Lattice (hep-lat) category contains only papers with latest versions from 2018 or later (new submissions, replacements, and cross-lists announced that month). Consequently, none of those articles have PS versions available.\n\n0", "expected": "31", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "2", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": null, "fb_mode": "gold", "code_rev": "3f7502f7.ff40ae22", "critic_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "guarded", "score_provenance": "gold", "judge_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "protocol_hash": "cda8cfafe9da", "prof_total_s": 579.25, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 579.25, "prof_tok_in": 525, "prof_tok_out": 11394, "prof_llm_calls": 2}
