{"timestamp": "2026-07-28T14:54:43.063634", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "no_mem", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_b7f857e4-d8aa-4387-af2a-0e844df5b9d8", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: The attached image contains a Python script. Run the Python code against an array of strings, listed below. The output of the Python script will be a URL containing C++ source code. Compile and run this C++ code against the array [35, 12, 8, 99, 21, 5] and return the sum of the third and fifth integers in the sorted list.\n\narr = ['_alg', 'ghi', 'C++', 'jkl', 'tps', '/Q', 'pqr', 'stu', ':', '//', 'rose', 'vwx', 'yz1', '234', 'tta', '567', '890'", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "The Python script rearranges the provided string fragments to form a URL pointing to a C++ sorting program. Compiling and running that program on the integer array [35, 12, 8, 99, 21, 5] sorts it in ascending order to [5, 8, 12, 21, 35, 99]. The third integer is 12 and the fifth is 35, so their sum is 47.\n\n47", "expected": "47", "score": 1.0, "em": 1.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "2", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": null, "fb_mode": "gold", "code_rev": "3f7502f7.ff40ae22", "critic_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "guarded", "score_provenance": "gold", "judge_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "protocol_hash": "cda8cfafe9da", "prof_total_s": 837.73, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 837.73, "prof_tok_in": 871, "prof_tok_out": 28909, "prof_llm_calls": 2}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-28T14:55:13.364930", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "no_mem", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_114d5fd0-e2ae-4b6d-a65a-870da2d19c08", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: In the endnote found in the second-to-last paragraph of page 11 of the book with the doi 10.2307/j.ctv9b2xdv, what date in November was the Wikipedia article accessed? Just give the day of the month.", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "The book with DOI 10.2307/j.ctv9b2xdv includes an endnote in the second-to-last paragraph of page 11 that cites a Wikipedia article. The access date recorded in that endnote is in November, specifically the 14th.\n\n14", "expected": "4", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "2", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": null, "fb_mode": "gold", "code_rev": "3f7502f7.ff40ae22", "critic_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "guarded", "score_provenance": "gold", "judge_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "protocol_hash": "cda8cfafe9da", "prof_total_s": 569.88, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 569.88, "prof_tok_in": 589, "prof_tok_out": 8470, "prof_llm_calls": 2}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-28T14:55:23.978955", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "no_mem", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_708b99c5-e4a7-49cb-a5cf-933c8d46470d", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: On the DeepFruits fruit detection graph on Connected Papers from 2016, what feature caused the largest bubble to be the size it is?", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "On Connected Papers, the size of each node (bubble) is determined by the number of citations that paper has received. The largest bubble on the DeepFruits (2016) graph corresponds to the most-cited paper in the related works network, so its size is driven by its high citation count.\n\nThe number of citations (citation count) of the paper", "expected": "Citations", "score": 1.0, "em": 1.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "2", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 2, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": null, "fb_mode": "gold", "code_rev": "3f7502f7.ff40ae22", "critic_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "guarded", "score_provenance": "gold", "judge_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "protocol_hash": "cda8cfafe9da", "prof_total_s": 625.56, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 625.56, "prof_tok_in": 537, "prof_tok_out": 2575, "prof_llm_calls": 2}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-28T14:55:25.565809", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "no_mem", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_20194330-9976-4043-8632-f8485c6c71b2", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: The YouTube channel Game Grumps began a Let’s Play of the game Sonic the Hedgehog (2006) in the year 2012. Thirty seconds into the first episode, a phrase is shown on the screen in white letters on a red background. How many times does the letter \"E\" appear in this phrase?", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "The phrase shown is “THIS GAME IS A PIECE OF SHIT.” Counting the letter “E”: GAME (1), PIECE (2) → total 3.\n\n3", "expected": "4", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "2", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": null, "fb_mode": "gold", "code_rev": "3f7502f7.ff40ae22", "critic_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "guarded", "score_provenance": "gold", "judge_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "protocol_hash": "cda8cfafe9da", "prof_total_s": 536.37, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 536.37, "prof_tok_in": 613, "prof_tok_out": 5883, "prof_llm_calls": 2}
