{"timestamp": "2026-07-28T14:57:05.055897", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "no_mem", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_08cae58d-4084-4616-b6dd-dd6534e4825b", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: According to Google Finance, when was the first year the Apple stock went above $50 (without adjusting for stock split)?", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "Apple’s stock (AAPL) debuted at $22 in December 1980 and traded mostly in the $15–$40 range through the mid‑1980s. It did not close above $50 in the early 1980s (peaking around $37 in 1983) or in 1986 (roughly $30–$40). In 1987, ahead of its first 2‑for‑1 stock split that June, the nominal share price rose above $50 (reaching roughly $80 pre‑split). Thus, the first year Apple’s unadjusted stock price exceeded $50 was 1987.\n\n1987", "expected": "2018", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "2", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": null, "fb_mode": "gold", "code_rev": "3f7502f7.ff40ae22", "critic_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "guarded", "score_provenance": "gold", "judge_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "protocol_hash": "cda8cfafe9da", "prof_total_s": 637.03, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 637.03, "prof_tok_in": 527, "prof_tok_out": 12054, "prof_llm_calls": 2}
