{"timestamp": "2026-07-28T14:59:12.979776", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "no_mem", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_ad37a656-079a-49f9-a493-7b739c9167d1", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: On July 15, 2008, Phys.org published an article about a catastrophe. Find the explosive force of this catastrophe according to Encyclopedia Britannica, then find the name of the US nuclear test that had the same yield. Your answer should only be the last word of the name of the test.", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "The Phys.org article published on July 15, 2008, covered the Tunguska catastrophe. According to Encyclopedia Britannica, the explosive force of the Tunguska event was approximately 15 megatons of TNT. The U.S. nuclear test that had the same yield was Castle Bravo. The last word of that test's name is:\n\nBravo", "expected": "Bravo", "score": 1.0, "em": 1.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "2", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 2, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": null, "fb_mode": "gold", "code_rev": "3f7502f7.ff40ae22", "critic_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "guarded", "score_provenance": "gold", "judge_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "protocol_hash": "cda8cfafe9da", "prof_total_s": 697.54, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 697.54, "prof_tok_in": 599, "prof_tok_out": 5987, "prof_llm_calls": 2}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-28T14:59:16.140621", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "no_mem", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_3ff6b7a9-a5bd-4412-ad92-0cd0d45c0fee", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: The longest-lived vertebrate is named after an island.  According to Wikipedia as of January 1, 2021, what is the 2020 estimated population of that island, to the nearest thousand?", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "The longest-lived vertebrate is the Greenland shark, named after Greenland. Wikipedia’s 2020 population estimate for Greenland was about 56,000 (roughly 56,081), which rounds to the nearest thousand as:\n\n56,000", "expected": "56000", "score": 1.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "2", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": null, "fb_mode": "gold", "code_rev": "3f7502f7.ff40ae22", "critic_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "guarded", "score_provenance": "gold", "judge_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "protocol_hash": "cda8cfafe9da", "prof_total_s": 648.61, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 648.61, "prof_tok_in": 561, "prof_tok_out": 3834, "prof_llm_calls": 2}
