{"timestamp": "2026-07-28T14:59:18.080822", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "no_mem", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_4d0aa727-86b1-406b-9b33-f870dd14a4a5", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: The attached file lists the locomotives owned by a local railroad museum. It gives each locomotive’s identifying number, operating status, and the name of the daily excursion it heads, if operational. What are the odds that today’s Sunset Picnic Trip will use a steam locomotive? Assume that each day’s excursion picks one of its assigned locomotives at random, and express the answer in the form “1 in 4”, “1 in 5”, etc.", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "</think:6124c78e>I'll start by exploring the environment to find the attached file.</think:6124c78e>```python\nimport os\nimport glob\n\n# List files in current directory and subdirectories\nfor root, dirs, files in os.walk('.'):\n    for f in files:\n        print(os.path.join(root, f))\n```", "expected": "1 in 3", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "2", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 0, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": null, "fb_mode": "gold", "code_rev": "3f7502f7.ff40ae22", "critic_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "guarded", "score_provenance": "gold", "judge_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "protocol_hash": "cda8cfafe9da", "prof_total_s": 1157.94, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 1157.94, "prof_tok_in": 320, "prof_tok_out": 426, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
