{"timestamp": "2026-07-28T15:00:06.755849", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "no_mem", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_935e2cff-ae78-4218-b3f5-115589b19dae", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: In the year 2022, and before December, what does \"R\" stand for in the three core policies of the type of content that was violated in the public logs on the Legume Wikipedia page?", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "The three core content policies on Wikipedia are Neutral point of view, Verifiability, and No original research (NOR). In that context, the \"R\" stands for Research.\n\nResearch", "expected": "research", "score": 1.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "1", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 2, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": null, "fb_mode": "gold", "code_rev": "3f7502f7.ff40ae22", "critic_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "guarded", "score_provenance": "gold", "judge_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "protocol_hash": "cda8cfafe9da", "prof_total_s": 690.02, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 690.02, "prof_tok_in": 563, "prof_tok_out": 5446, "prof_llm_calls": 2}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-28T15:00:17.478365", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "no_mem", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_50ec8903-b81f-4257-9450-1085afd2c319", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: A standard Rubik’s cube has been broken into cubes making up its sides. The cubes are jumbled, and one is removed. There are 6 cubes with one colored face, 12 edge cubes with two colored faces, and 8 corner cubes with three colored faces. All blue cubes have been found. All cubes directly left, right, above, and below the orange center cube have been found, along with the center cube. The green corners have all been found, along with all green", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "green, white", "expected": "green, white", "score": 1.0, "em": 1.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "1", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": null, "fb_mode": "gold", "code_rev": "3f7502f7.ff40ae22", "critic_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "guarded", "score_provenance": "gold", "judge_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "protocol_hash": "cda8cfafe9da", "prof_total_s": 933.6, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 933.6, "prof_tok_in": 777, "prof_tok_out": 24420, "prof_llm_calls": 2}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-28T15:00:19.368262", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "no_mem", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_9e1fc53b-46ff-49a1-9d05-9e6faac34cc5", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: A 5-man group made up of one tank, one healer, and three DPS is doing a dungeon that was just released in World of Warcraft. Two are plate wearers and two are cloth wearers. At the final boss, both the tank and the healer are casting holy spells. Ice and fire are being used, each one by a different DPS. A bear from the group is attacking the boss. Metamorphosis is cast. The Kilt of the Forgotten One drops as loot, but no one can use it. If all", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "Death Knight, Druid, Paladin, Priest, Warlock", "expected": "Death Knight, Hunter, Paladin, Priest, Warlock", "score": 0.8, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "3", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": null, "fb_mode": "gold", "code_rev": "3f7502f7.ff40ae22", "critic_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "guarded", "score_provenance": "gold", "judge_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "protocol_hash": "cda8cfafe9da", "prof_total_s": 780.66, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 780.66, "prof_tok_in": 769, "prof_tok_out": 15973, "prof_llm_calls": 2}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-28T15:01:12.987442", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "no_mem", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_7dd30055-0198-452e-8c25-f73dbe27dcb8", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: Using the Biopython library in Python, parse the PDB file of the protein identified by the PDB ID 5wb7 from the RCSB Protein Data Bank. Calculate the distance between the first and second atoms as they are listed in the PDB file. Report the answer in Angstroms, rounded to the nearest picometer.", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "```python\nimport urllib.request, os, sys, subprocess, json, math\n\n# Ensure Biopython is available\ntry:\n    import Bio\nexcept ImportError:\n    subprocess.check_call([sys.executable, '-m', 'pip', 'install', 'biopython', '-q'])\n\nfrom Bio.PDB import PDBParser\n\nurl = 'https://files.rcsb.org/download/5wb7.pdb'\npdb_file = '5wb7.pdb'\nurllib.request.urlretrieve(url, pdb_file)\n\n# Inspect first few lines of raw file\nwith open(pdb_file) as f:\n    lines = f.readlines()\nprint(''.join(lines[:20]))\n```\n\n```python\n# Parse with Biopython\nparser = PDBParser(QUIET=True)\nstructure = parser.get_structure('5wb7', pdb_file)\n\n# Collect atoms in order as they appear in the file (all models)\natoms = []\nfor model in structure:\n    for chain in model:\n        for residue in chain:\n            for atom in residue:\n                atoms.append(atom)\n\nprint('Total atoms parsed:', len(atoms))\nfor i, atom in enumerate(atoms[:5]):\n    print(i, atom.get_parent().get_resname(), atom.get_name(), atom.get_serial_number(), atom.coord)\n\n# First and second atoms\na1 = atoms[0]\na2 = atoms[1]\ncoord1 = a1.coord\ncoord2 = a2.coord\ndist = math.sqrt(((coord1-coord2)**2).sum())\nprint('Distance (A):', dist)\nprint('Rounded to nearest 0.01 A (pm):', round(dist, 2))\n```\n\n```python\n# Also verify by directly parsing ATOM/HETATM lines in file order\nimport re\nfile_atoms = []\nfor line in lines:\n    if line.startswith('ATOM') or line.startswith('HETATM'):\n        # columns: serial 7-11, x 31-38, y 39-46, z 47-54\n        serial = int(line[6:11])\n        x = float(line[30:38]); y = float(line[38:46]); z = float(line[46:54])\n        file_atoms.append((serial, x, y, z))\nprint('File atom lines:', len(file_atoms))\nprint('First two file atoms:', file_atoms[:2])\ndx = file_atoms[1][1]-file_atoms[0][1]\ndy = file_atoms[1][2]-file_atoms[0][2]\ndz = file_atoms[1][3]-file_atoms[0][3]\ndist_direct = math.sqrt(dx*dx+dy*dy+dz*dz)\nprint('Direct distance:', dist_direct)\nprint('Rounded:', round(dist_direct,2))\n```\n\n```python\n# Check if there are multiple models and whether first two atoms are within first model\nmodels = list(structure)\nprint('Number of models:', len(models))\n# Print first two atom serials from first model using Biopython\nfirst_model_atoms = []\nfor chain in models[0]:\n    for residue in chain:\n        for atom in residue:\n            first_model_atoms.append(atom)\nprint('First model atoms count:', len(first_model_atoms))\nprint('First two in first model:', first_model_atoms[0].get_serial_number(), first_model_atoms[1].get_serial_number())\n```\n\n```python\n# Final answer rounding to nearest picometer (0.01 A)\nfinal = round(dist_direct, 2)\nprint('FINAL', final)\n```", "expected": "1.456", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "2", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 2, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": null, "fb_mode": "gold", "code_rev": "3f7502f7.ff40ae22", "critic_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "guarded", "score_provenance": "gold", "judge_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "protocol_hash": "cda8cfafe9da", "prof_total_s": 628.5, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 628.5, "prof_tok_in": 294, "prof_tok_out": 1258, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-28T15:01:20.440586", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "no_mem", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_a0c07678-e491-4bbc-8f0b-07405144218f", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: Who are the pitchers with the number before and after Taishō Tamai's number as of July 2023? Give them to me in the form Pitcher Before, Pitcher After, use their last names only, in Roman characters.", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "Taishō Tamai (Hokkaido Nippon-Ham Fighters) wore jersey number 17 as of July 2023. The pitcher with number 16 was Kohei Arihara, and the pitcher with number 18 was Kosei Yoshida.\n\nArihara, Yoshida", "expected": "Yoshida, Uehara", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "1", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": null, "fb_mode": "gold", "code_rev": "3f7502f7.ff40ae22", "critic_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "guarded", "score_provenance": "gold", "judge_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "protocol_hash": "cda8cfafe9da", "prof_total_s": 777.33, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 777.33, "prof_tok_in": 579, "prof_tok_out": 11374, "prof_llm_calls": 2}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-28T15:01:27.973041", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "no_mem", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_3cef3a44-215e-4aed-8e3b-b1e3f08063b7", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: I'm making a grocery list for my mom, but she's a professor of botany and she's a real stickler when it comes to categorizing things. I need to add different foods to different categories on the grocery list, but if I make a mistake, she won't buy anything inserted in the wrong category. Here's the list I have so far:\n\nmilk, eggs, flour, whole bean coffee, Oreos, sweet potatoes, fresh basil, plums, green beans, rice, corn, bell pepper, whole a", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "To classify these grocery items for a botany professor, we must use strict botanical definitions: fruits develop from the flower's ovary and contain seeds, while vegetables are other edible plant parts (roots, stems, leaves, flowers). Seeds, grains, and nuts are not botanical vegetables.\n\n- sweet potatoes: tuberous root → vegetable  \n- fresh basil: leaves → vegetable  \n- broccoli: flower clusters → vegetable  \n- celery: petioles (stems) → vegetable  \n- lettuce: leaves → vegetable  \n- plums, green beans, rice, corn, bell pepper, whole allspice, acorns, zucchini, peanuts: botanical fruits (or seeds/fruits) → exclude  \n- whole bean coffee: seed → not a vegetable  \n- milk, eggs, flour, Oreos: non-plant → exclude  \n\nAlphabetizing the vegetables yields: broccoli, celery, fresh basil, lettuce, sweet potatoes.\n\nbroccoli, celery, fresh basil, lettuce, sweet potatoes", "expected": "broccoli, celery, fresh basil, lettuce, sweet potatoes", "score": 1.0, "em": 1.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "1", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 2, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": null, "fb_mode": "gold", "code_rev": "3f7502f7.ff40ae22", "critic_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "guarded", "score_provenance": "gold", "judge_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "protocol_hash": "cda8cfafe9da", "prof_total_s": 728.93, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 728.93, "prof_tok_in": 941, "prof_tok_out": 5638, "prof_llm_calls": 2}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-28T15:01:34.693614", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "no_mem", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_04a04a9b-226c-43fd-b319-d5e89743676f", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: If we assume all articles published by Nature in 2020 (articles, only, not book reviews/columns, etc) relied on statistical significance to justify their findings and they on average came to a p-value of 0.04, how many papers would be incorrect as to their claims of statistical significance? Round the value up to the next integer.", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "Nature published approximately 1,145 research articles in 2020 (excluding book reviews, columns, etc.). Treating the average p‑value of 0.04 as the expected false‑positive rate gives 1,145 × 0.04 = 45.8, which rounds up to the next integer:\n\n46", "expected": "41", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "2", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": null, "fb_mode": "gold", "code_rev": "3f7502f7.ff40ae22", "critic_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "guarded", "score_provenance": "gold", "judge_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "protocol_hash": "cda8cfafe9da", "prof_total_s": 828.47, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 828.47, "prof_tok_in": 621, "prof_tok_out": 14339, "prof_llm_calls": 2}
