{"timestamp": "2026-07-28T15:02:43.088433", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "no_mem", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_853c8244-429e-46ca-89f2-addf40dfb2bd", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: In the 2015 Metropolitan Museum of Art exhibition titled after the Chinese zodiac animal of 2015, how many of the \"twelve animals of the Chinese zodiac\" have a hand visible?", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "The 2015 Met exhibition was “The Year of the Sheep” (also referred to as the Year of the Goat/Ram). Within it, the group of works called “The Twelve Animals of the Chinese Zodiac” are the Tang‑dynasty style zodiac figures (human bodies with animal heads), each shown with hands clasped in front. Thus, all twelve depictions have a hand visible.\n\n12", "expected": "11", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "2", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": null, "fb_mode": "gold", "code_rev": "3f7502f7.ff40ae22", "critic_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "guarded", "score_provenance": "gold", "judge_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "protocol_hash": "cda8cfafe9da", "prof_total_s": 959.23, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 959.23, "prof_tok_in": 557, "prof_tok_out": 23144, "prof_llm_calls": 2}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-28T15:02:43.773566", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "no_mem", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_56db2318-640f-477a-a82f-bc93ad13e882", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: The following numbers function similarly to ISBN 13 numbers, however, their validation methods are slightly different. Rather than using alternate weights of 1 and 3, the checksum digit is calculated with an alternate weight of 1 and some other positive integer less than 10. Otherwise, the checksum digit is calculated as expected. Unfortunately, there is an error in the data. Two adjacent columns have been transposed. These errored columns do ", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "7, 9", "expected": "7, 9", "score": 1.0, "em": 1.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "3", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 2, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": null, "fb_mode": "gold", "code_rev": "3f7502f7.ff40ae22", "critic_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "guarded", "score_provenance": "gold", "judge_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "protocol_hash": "cda8cfafe9da", "prof_total_s": 1046.27, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 1046.27, "prof_tok_in": 469, "prof_tok_out": 29614, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-28T15:02:45.436164", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "no_mem", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_a3fbeb63-0e8c-4a11-bff6-0e3b484c3e9c", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: How many slides in this PowerPoint presentation mention crustaceans?", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "I have not been provided with any PowerPoint file, slide content, or reference to a specific presentation in this conversation. Since no such document is available and no tools can be used to access one, it is impossible to examine slides for mentions of crustaceans.\n\nUnable to determine (no presentation provided)", "expected": "4", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "1", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 2, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": null, "fb_mode": "gold", "code_rev": "3f7502f7.ff40ae22", "critic_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "guarded", "score_provenance": "gold", "judge_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "protocol_hash": "cda8cfafe9da", "prof_total_s": 612.2, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 612.2, "prof_tok_in": 499, "prof_tok_out": 1292, "prof_llm_calls": 2}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-28T15:02:49.992674", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "no_mem", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_27d5d136-8563-469e-92bf-fd103c28b57c", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: ¬(A ∧ B) ↔ (¬A ∨ ¬B)\n¬(A ∨ B) ↔ (¬A ∧ ¬B)\n(A → B) ↔ (¬B → ¬A)\n(A → B) ↔ (¬A ∨ B)\n(¬A → B) ↔ (A ∨ ¬B)\n¬(A → B) ↔ (A ∧ ¬B)\n\nWhich of the above is not logically equivalent to the rest? Provide the full statement that doesn't fit.", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "```python\nimport itertools\n\ndef eval_expr(A,B,num):\n    if num==1:\n        return (not (A and B)) == ((not A) or (not B))\n    if num==2:\n        return (not (A or B)) == ((not A) and (not B))\n    if num==3:\n        return ((not A) or B) == ((not (not B)) or (not A))  # A->B vs ¬B->¬A\n    if num==4:\n        return ((not A) or B) == ((not A) or B)\n    if num==5:\n        # (¬A → B) ↔ (A ∨ ¬B)\n        lhs = (not (not A)) or B  # ¬A -> B = A or B\n        rhs = A or (not B)\n        return lhs == rhs\n    if num==6:\n        # ¬(A → B) ↔ (A ∧ ¬B)\n        lhs = not ((not A) or B)\n        rhs = A and (not B)\n        return lhs == rhs\n\nfor num in range(1,7):\n    results=[]\n    for A,B in itertools.product([True,False],repeat=2):\n        results.append(eval_expr(A,B,num))\n    print(num, results, all(results))\n```</think:6124c78e>```python\nfor num in range(1,7):\n    results=[]\n    for A,B in itertools.product([True,False],repeat=2):\n        results.append(eval_expr(A,B,num))\n    print(num, all(results))\n```", "expected": "(¬A → B) ↔ (A ∨ ¬B)", "score": 1.0, "em": 1.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "1", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 2, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": null, "fb_mode": "gold", "code_rev": "3f7502f7.ff40ae22", "critic_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "guarded", "score_provenance": "gold", "judge_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "protocol_hash": "cda8cfafe9da", "prof_total_s": 563.28, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 563.28, "prof_tok_in": 322, "prof_tok_out": 1160, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
