{"timestamp": "2026-07-28T15:06:01.056111", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "no_mem", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_b7f857e4-d8aa-4387-af2a-0e844df5b9d8", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: The attached image contains a Python script. Run the Python code against an array of strings, listed below. The output of the Python script will be a URL containing C++ source code. Compile and run this C++ code against the array [35, 12, 8, 99, 21, 5] and return the sum of the third and fifth integers in the sorted list.\n\narr = ['_alg', 'ghi', 'C++', 'jkl', 'tps', '/Q', 'pqr', 'stu', ':', '//', 'rose', 'vwx', 'yz1', '234', 'tta', '567', '890'", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "```python\nimport urllib.request, re, sys, json, textwrap, os\n\nurl = \"https://rosettacode.org/wiki/Sorting_algorithms/Quicksort\"\ntry:\n    data = urllib.request.urlopen(url, timeout=15).read().decode('utf-8')\n    print(\"Fetched length:\", len(data))\n    # Find C++ section\n    # MediaWiki sections: <span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"C.2B.2B\">C++</span> or id=\"C++\"\n    match = re.search(r'id=\"(C\\+\\+|C\\.2B\\.2B)\"(.*?)(<span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"|</div>)', data, re.DOTALL)\n    if match:\n        print(\"Found C++ section\")\n        snippet = match.group(0)[:2000]\n        print(snippet)\n    else:\n        print(\"No C++ section found, searching for 'C++'\")\n        idx = data.find('C++')\n        print(data[idx-200:idx+800])\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print(\"Error:\", e)\n```", "expected": "47", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "2", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 2, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": null, "fb_mode": "gold", "code_rev": "3f7502f7.ff40ae22", "critic_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "guarded", "score_provenance": "gold", "judge_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "protocol_hash": "cda8cfafe9da", "prof_total_s": 610.0, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 610.0, "prof_tok_in": 420, "prof_tok_out": 7540, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-28T15:06:12.286473", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "no_mem", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_4d0aa727-86b1-406b-9b33-f870dd14a4a5", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: The attached file lists the locomotives owned by a local railroad museum. It gives each locomotive’s identifying number, operating status, and the name of the daily excursion it heads, if operational. What are the odds that today’s Sunset Picnic Trip will use a steam locomotive? Assume that each day’s excursion picks one of its assigned locomotives at random, and express the answer in the form “1 in 4”, “1 in 5”, etc.", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "I'll start by checking if there's an attached file in the working directory that I can read.</think:6124c78e>```python\nimport os\nimport glob\n\n# List files in current directory and common locations\nprint(\"Current directory:\", os.getcwd())\nprint(\"Files in current directory:\")\nfor f in os.listdir('.'):\n    print(f)\nprint(\"\\nSearching for any data files...\")\nfor ext in ['*', '*.txt', '*.csv', '*.json', '*.xlsx', '*.pdf']:\n    for f in glob.glob(ext):\n        print(f)\n```", "expected": "1 in 3", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "2", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": null, "fb_mode": "gold", "code_rev": "3f7502f7.ff40ae22", "critic_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "guarded", "score_provenance": "gold", "judge_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "protocol_hash": "cda8cfafe9da", "prof_total_s": 344.32, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 344.32, "prof_tok_in": 320, "prof_tok_out": 569, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-28T15:06:40.340767", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "no_mem", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_08cae58d-4084-4616-b6dd-dd6534e4825b", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: According to Google Finance, when was the first year the Apple stock went above $50 (without adjusting for stock split)?", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "Apple Inc. (AAPL) went public in December 1980 at $22 per share. Its first stock split (2-for-1) did not occur until 1987. On a non-split-adjusted basis, historical price records (including Google Finance’s unadjusted data) show that Apple’s stock first traded above $50 in 1983, reaching a high of over $60 that year. Therefore, the first year the stock went above $50 without adjusting for splits was:\n\n1983", "expected": "2018", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "2", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 2, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": null, "fb_mode": "gold", "code_rev": "3f7502f7.ff40ae22", "critic_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "guarded", "score_provenance": "gold", "judge_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "protocol_hash": "cda8cfafe9da", "prof_total_s": 487.47, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 487.47, "prof_tok_in": 527, "prof_tok_out": 5886, "prof_llm_calls": 2}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-28T15:06:52.287110", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "no_mem", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_0bdb7c40-671d-4ad1-9ce3-986b159c0ddc", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: In NASA's Astronomy Picture of the Day on 2006 January 21, two astronauts are visible, with one appearing much smaller than the other. As of August 2023, out of the astronauts in the NASA Astronaut Group that the smaller astronaut was a member of, which one spent the least time in space, and how many minutes did he spend in space, rounded to the nearest minute? Exclude any astronauts who did not spend any time in space. Give the last name of t", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "Jemison; 11430", "expected": "White; 5876", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "3", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": null, "fb_mode": "gold", "code_rev": "3f7502f7.ff40ae22", "critic_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "guarded", "score_provenance": "gold", "judge_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "protocol_hash": "cda8cfafe9da", "prof_total_s": 1085.14, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 1085.14, "prof_tok_in": 705, "prof_tok_out": 31357, "prof_llm_calls": 2}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-28T15:06:54.107315", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "no_mem", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_3ff6b7a9-a5bd-4412-ad92-0cd0d45c0fee", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: The longest-lived vertebrate is named after an island.  According to Wikipedia as of January 1, 2021, what is the 2020 estimated population of that island, to the nearest thousand?", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "The longest-lived vertebrate is the Greenland shark, named after Greenland. Wikipedia's Greenland page as of January 1, 2021 listed the 2020 estimated population as 56,081, which rounds to the nearest thousand as 56,000.\n\n56,000", "expected": "56000", "score": 1.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "2", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 2, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": null, "fb_mode": "gold", "code_rev": "3f7502f7.ff40ae22", "critic_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "guarded", "score_provenance": "gold", "judge_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "protocol_hash": "cda8cfafe9da", "prof_total_s": 362.76, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 362.76, "prof_tok_in": 561, "prof_tok_out": 2913, "prof_llm_calls": 2}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-28T15:06:55.598129", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "no_mem", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_7b5377b0-3f38-4103-8ad2-90fe89864c04", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: Find the value of x to the nearest tenth: Lx = (d/dx * (A * x-squared)) + 4-thousand'n'ninety-7 minus C\nWhere L is the last two digits of the year of the Venezuelan Declaration of Independence,\nA is the number of colors in the TikTok logo as of July 2023, excluding black and white,\nand C is the height of the average woman in the Philippines according to a July 2023 Business Insider article, rounded to the nearest whole centimeter", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "Venezuelan Declaration of Independence: 1811 → L = 11.\nTikTok logo colors (excluding black/white): cyan and magenta → A = 2.\nAverage height of women in the Philippines (Business Insider July 2023): 149.6 cm → rounded C = 150.\n\nEquation: Lx = d/dx(A·x²) + 4097 − C\n11x = 2·2·x + 4097 − 150\n11x = 4x + 3947\n7x = 3947\nx = 3947 ÷ 7 ≈ 563.857...\n\nRounded to the nearest tenth: 563.9\n\n563.9", "expected": "563.9", "score": 1.0, "em": 1.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "2", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": null, "fb_mode": "gold", "code_rev": "3f7502f7.ff40ae22", "critic_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "guarded", "score_provenance": "gold", "judge_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "protocol_hash": "cda8cfafe9da", "prof_total_s": 280.35, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 280.35, "prof_tok_in": 695, "prof_tok_out": 4607, "prof_llm_calls": 2}
