{"timestamp": "2026-07-28T15:14:31.090598", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "no_mem", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_384d0dd8-e8a4-4cfe-963c-d37f256e7662", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: In the NCATS PubChem compound database for Food Additive Status classification, find the compound that has a molecular weight of 100 g/mol or less, 6 heavy atoms, 1 or fewer hydrogen bond acceptors, and a complexity between 10 and 15. Of the shared gene-chemical co-occurrences between its two possible enzyme transformations, what is the PubChem CID of the heaviest by molecular weight?", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "The compound matching the filters is benzene (CID 241). Its two enzyme transformations share cofactors such as O₂, H₂O, and NADPH; the heaviest chemical among the shared gene‑chemical co‑occurrences is NADPH.\n\n5888", "expected": "4192", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "3", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 2, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": null, "fb_mode": "gold", "code_rev": "3f7502f7.ff40ae22", "critic_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "guarded", "score_provenance": "gold", "judge_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "protocol_hash": "cda8cfafe9da", "prof_total_s": 439.53, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 439.53, "prof_tok_in": 651, "prof_tok_out": 21359, "prof_llm_calls": 2}
