{"timestamp": "2026-07-28T15:26:30.351956", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "no_mem", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_a26649c6-1cb2-470a-871e-6910c64c3e53", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: What is the absolute difference in tens of thousands between the population of chinstrap penguins on the Wikipedia page for penguin species populations as of the end of 2018 and the population recorded in the Nature.com \"global population assessment of the Chinstrap penguin\" article from 2020, assuming two penguins per breeding pair?", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "The Wikipedia page for penguin species populations (List of penguins / Penguin species table) as of end of 2018 lists the Chinstrap penguin population at approximately 8,000,000 individuals. The Nature.com 2020 global population assessment (Lynch et al., Scientific Reports) estimates 3,420,000 breeding pairs; assuming two penguins per pair gives 6,840,000 individuals. The absolute difference is |8,000,000 − 6,840,000| = 1,160,000. Expressed in tens of thousands, this is 1,160,000 ÷ 10,000 = 116.\n\n116", "expected": "116", "score": 1.0, "em": 1.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "2", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": null, "fb_mode": "gold", "code_rev": "3f7502f7.ff40ae22", "critic_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "guarded", "score_provenance": "gold", "judge_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "protocol_hash": "cda8cfafe9da", "prof_total_s": 1420.18, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 1420.18, "prof_tok_in": 609, "prof_tok_out": 5840, "prof_llm_calls": 2}
