{"timestamp": "2026-07-28T21:03:02.722552", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "amem", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_50ec8903-b81f-4257-9450-1085afd2c319", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: A standard Rubik’s cube has been broken into cubes making up its sides. The cubes are jumbled, and one is removed. There are 6 cubes with one colored face, 12 edge cubes with two colored faces, and 8 corner cubes with three colored faces. All blue cubes have been found. All cubes directly left, right, above, and below the orange center cube have been found, along with the center cube. The green corners have all been found, along with all green", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "Standard Rubik’s cube opposite pairs are white–yellow, red–orange, blue–green.  \nEdges are the 12 non‑opposite color pairs.\n\n- All blue pieces found ⇒ blue edges (white‑blue, yellow‑blue, red‑blue, orange‑blue) are found.  \n- The orange center and the four cubes orthogonally adjacent to it are found ⇒ orange edges with white, yellow, blue, green are found.  \n- Green corners all found include the orange‑green and blue‑green corners, so every orange piece (center, 4 edges, 4 corners) is found.  \n- Therefore the pieces on the opposite (red) face are all found ⇒ red edges with white, yellow, blue, green are found.  \n- “All green that borders yellow” gives the green‑yellow edge.\n\nListing all 12 edges, the only one not covered by the above is the white‑green edge. Since the missing cube is an edge, its two colors are green and white, ordered alphabetically.\n\ngreen, white", "expected": "green, white", "score": 1.0, "em": 1.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "1", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 0, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 1.0, "fb_mode": "gold", "code_rev": "56816631.fcf27e88", "critic_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "guarded", "score_provenance": "gold", "judge_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "protocol_hash": "65cea4ee79fd", "prof_total_s": 525.34, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 525.34, "prof_tok_in": 777, "prof_tok_out": 23326, "prof_llm_calls": 2}
