{"timestamp": "2026-07-28T21:06:36.718462", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "amem", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_ad37a656-079a-49f9-a493-7b739c9167d1", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: On July 15, 2008, Phys.org published an article about a catastrophe. Find the explosive force of this catastrophe according to Encyclopedia Britannica, then find the name of the US nuclear test that had the same yield. Your answer should only be the last word of the name of the test.", "augmented_prompt": "## Memories from earlier attempts (A-Mem)\n\n- Task: Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: On July 15, 2008, Phys.org published an article about a catastrophe. Find the explosive force of this catastrophe according to Encyclopedia Britannica, then find the name of the US nuclear test that had the same yield. Your answer should only be the last word of the name of the test.\nAttempt: Bravo", "response": "The July 15, 2008 Phys.org article concerns the Tunguska catastrophe. Encyclopedia Britannica gives its explosive force as about 10–15 megatons of TNT (commonly cited as ~15 Mt). The U.S. nuclear test with that yield was Castle Bravo. The last word of the test name is:\n\nBravo", "expected": "Bravo", "score": 1.0, "em": 1.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "2", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 403, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 1.0, "fb_mode": "gold", "code_rev": "56816631.fcf27e88", "critic_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "guarded", "score_provenance": "gold", "judge_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "protocol_hash": "65cea4ee79fd", "prof_total_s": 550.38, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 550.38, "prof_tok_in": 773, "prof_tok_out": 3270, "prof_llm_calls": 2}
