{"timestamp": "2026-07-28T21:10:25.879173", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "amem", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_7d4a7d1d-cac6-44a8-96e8-ea9584a70825", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: According to Girls Who Code, how long did it take in years for the percentage of computer scientists that were women to change by 13% from a starting point of 37%?", "augmented_prompt": "## Memories from earlier attempts (A-Mem)\n\n- Task: Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: According to Girls Who Code, how long did it take in years for the percentage of computer scientists that were women to change by 13% from a starting point of 37%?\nAttempt: Girls Who Code cites that in 1984, 37% of computer scientists were women, and that by 2014 this had dropped to 24% — a change of 13 percentage points. The elapsed time ", "response": "Girls Who Code reports that in 1984, 37% of computer scientists were women, and by 2014 that share had fallen to 24%—a drop of 13 percentage points. The time span from 1984 to 2014 is 2014 − 1984 = 30 years.\n\n30 years", "expected": "22", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "1", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 445, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 0.0, "fb_mode": "gold", "code_rev": "56816631.fcf27e88", "critic_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "guarded", "score_provenance": "gold", "judge_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "protocol_hash": "65cea4ee79fd", "prof_total_s": 579.72, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 579.72, "prof_tok_in": 765, "prof_tok_out": 969, "prof_llm_calls": 2}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-28T21:10:26.420609", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "amem", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_851e570a-e3de-4d84-bcfa-cc85578baa59", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: I thought we could try a fun word puzzle together :)\n\nI've got a Boggle board here:\n\nABRL\nEITE\nIONS\nFPEI\n\nI'd like to know the longest word that can be generated from the board. Please find the longest English language word that can be generated from this board. If more than one word of the same length exists at the maximum word length, please report the longest word that comes first, alphabetically. Oh, and I know that there might be differen", "augmented_prompt": "## Memories from earlier attempts (A-Mem)\n\n- Task: Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: I thought we could try a fun word puzzle together :)\n\nI've got a Boggle board here:\n\nABRL\nEITE\nIONS\nFPEI\n\nI'd like to know the longest word that can be generated from the board. Please find the longest English language word that can be generated from this board. If more than one word of the same length exists at the maximum word length, pl", "response": "```python\nimport requests, sys, time\n\nurl = \"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/dwyl/english-words/master/words_alpha.txt\"\nprint(\"Downloading dictionary...\")\nr = requests.get(url, timeout=30)\nprint(\"Status:\", r.status_code, \"len:\", len(r.text))\nwords = [w.strip().lower() for w in r.text.splitlines() if w.strip()]\nprint(\"Word count:\", len(words))\n\nboard = [\n    ['a','b','r','l'],\n    ['e','i','t','e'],\n    ['i','o','n','s'],\n    ['f','p','e','i']\n]\n\n# Build prefix set and word set\nword_set = set(words)\nprefix_set = set()\nfor w in words:\n    for i in range(1, len(w)+1):\n        prefix_set.add(w[:i])\n\n# Boggle search\nrows, cols = 4,4\nbest = []\n\ndef dfs(r, c, visited, path, word):\n    if word not in prefix_set:\n        return\n    if len(word) >= 3 and word in word_set:\n        best.append(word)\n    # continue longer\n    for dr in (-1,0,1):\n        for dc in (-1,0,1):\n            if dr==0 and dc==0: continue\n            nr, nc = r+dr, c+dc\n            if 0<=nr<rows and 0<=nc<cols and (nr,nc) not in visited:\n                dfs(nr, nc, visited | {(nr,nc)}, path+[ (nr,nc) ], word+board[nr][nc])\n\nfor r in range(rows):\n    for c in range(cols):\n        dfs(r, c, {(r,c)}, [(r,c)], board[r][c])\n\nprint(\"Found words count:\", len(best))\nif best:\n    maxlen = max(len(w) for w in best)\n    print(\"Max length:\", maxlen)\n    longest = sorted([w for w in best if len(w)==maxlen])\n    print(\"Longest words (alpha sorted):\", longest[:20])\n    print(\"Answer:\", longest[0])\n```\n\n```python\n# Let's also consider if min length 1 or 2 changes max; but check all lengths just in case\nbest_all = []\ndef dfs2(r, c, visited, word):\n    if word not in prefix_set:\n        return\n    if word in word_set:\n        best_all.append(word)\n    for dr in (-1,0,1):\n        for dc in (-1,0,1):\n            if dr==0 and dc==0: continue\n            nr, nc = r+dr, c+dc\n            if 0<=nr<rows and 0<=nc<cols and (nr,nc) not in visited:\n                dfs2(nr, nc, visited | {(nr,nc)}, word+board[nr][nc])\n\nfor r in range(rows):\n    for c in range(cols):\n        dfs2(r, c, {(r,c)}, board[r][c])\n\nmaxlen_all = max(len(w) for w in best_all)\nlongest_all = sorted([w for w in best_all if len(w)==maxlen_all])\nprint(\"All lengths max:\", maxlen_all, longest_all[:10])\n```", "expected": "Briniest", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "3", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 445, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 0.0, "fb_mode": "gold", "code_rev": "56816631.fcf27e88", "critic_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "guarded", "score_provenance": "gold", "judge_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "protocol_hash": "65cea4ee79fd", "prof_total_s": 551.26, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 551.26, "prof_tok_in": 465, "prof_tok_out": 1434, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-28T21:10:28.599296", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "amem", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_a0c07678-e491-4bbc-8f0b-07405144218f", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: Who are the pitchers with the number before and after Taishō Tamai's number as of July 2023? Give them to me in the form Pitcher Before, Pitcher After, use their last names only, in Roman characters.", "augmented_prompt": "## Memories from earlier attempts (A-Mem)\n\n- Task: Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: Who are the pitchers with the number before and after Taishō Tamai's number as of July 2023? Give them to me in the form Pitcher Before, Pitcher After, use their last names only, in Roman characters.\nAttempt: Taishō Tamai (玉井大翔) is a pitcher for the Hokkaido Nippon-Ham Fighters. As of July 2023, his jersey number is 57. On the same roster,", "response": "Takahashi, Watanabe", "expected": "Yoshida, Uehara", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "1", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 445, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 0.0, "fb_mode": "gold", "code_rev": "56816631.fcf27e88", "critic_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "guarded", "score_provenance": "gold", "judge_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "protocol_hash": "65cea4ee79fd", "prof_total_s": 676.28, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 676.28, "prof_tok_in": 821, "prof_tok_out": 6157, "prof_llm_calls": 2}
