{"timestamp": "2026-07-28T21:10:56.188983", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "amem", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_11af4e1a-5f45-467d-9aeb-46f4bb0bf034", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: How many more blocks (also denoted as layers) in BERT base encoder than the encoder from the architecture proposed in Attention is All You Need?", "augmented_prompt": "## Memories from earlier attempts (A-Mem)\n\n- Task: Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: How many more blocks (also denoted as layers) in BERT base encoder than the encoder from the architecture proposed in Attention is All You Need?\nAttempt: BERT-base uses 12 transformer encoder layers (blocks). The encoder in the original Transformer architecture from \"Attention is All You Need\" uses N = 6 layers. The difference is 12 − 6 = ", "response": "BERT-base encoder uses 12 layers. The encoder in \"Attention is All You Need\" uses N=6 layers. The difference is 12 - 6 = 6.\n\n6", "expected": "6", "score": 1.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "1", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 445, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 1.0, "fb_mode": "gold", "code_rev": "56816631.fcf27e88", "critic_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "guarded", "score_provenance": "gold", "judge_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "protocol_hash": "65cea4ee79fd", "prof_total_s": 544.38, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 544.38, "prof_tok_in": 731, "prof_tok_out": 913, "prof_llm_calls": 2}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-28T21:10:58.429933", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "amem", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_46719c30-f4c3-4cad-be07-d5cb21eee6bb", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: Of the authors (First M. Last) that worked on the paper \"Pie Menus or Linear Menus, Which Is Better?\" in 2015, what was the title of the first paper authored by the one that had authored prior papers?", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "The 2015 paper “Pie Menus or Linear Menus, Which Is Better?” was authored by Joey Scarr, Andy Cockburn, and Carl Gutwin. Among these, Andy Cockburn was the author with earlier prior publications, and his earliest paper is titled “A Predictive Model of Menu Performance.”\n\nA Predictive Model of Menu Performance", "expected": "Mapping Human Oriented Information to Software Agents for Online Systems Usage", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "1", "patch_injected": false, "aug_len": 0, "iteration": 0, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 0.0, "fb_mode": "gold", "code_rev": "56816631.fcf27e88", "critic_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "guarded", "score_provenance": "gold", "judge_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "protocol_hash": "65cea4ee79fd", "prof_total_s": 960.91, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 960.91, "prof_tok_in": 581, "prof_tok_out": 26026, "prof_llm_calls": 2}
