{"timestamp": "2026-07-28T21:12:40.928483", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "amem", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_2dfc4c37-fec1-4518-84a7-10095d30ad75", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: According to Box Office Mojo's 2020 Worldwide Box Office list, how many of the top 10 highest-grossing worldwide movies are also on the top 10 highest-grossing domestic movies? Your answer should be a numerical integer value.", "augmented_prompt": "## Memories from earlier attempts (A-Mem)\n\n- Task: Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: According to Box Office Mojo's 2020 Worldwide Box Office list, how many of the top 10 highest-grossing worldwide movies are also on the top 10 highest-grossing domestic movies? Your answer should be a numerical integer value.\nAttempt: Based on Box Office Mojo's 2020 calendar-year charts, the worldwide top 10 includes Bad Boys for Life, 191", "response": "Box Office Mojo’s 2020 worldwide top 10 includes several non‑US releases (Demon Slayer, The Eight Hundred, My People My Homeland, Jiang Ziya) that did not place in the US/Canada domestic top 10. The Hollywood titles that appear on both the worldwide top 10 and the domestic top 10 are: Bad Boys for Life, 1917, Tenet, Sonic the Hedgehog, Dolittle, and The Croods: A New Age.\n\n6", "expected": "6", "score": 1.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "2", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 445, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 1.0, "fb_mode": "gold", "code_rev": "56816631.fcf27e88", "critic_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "guarded", "score_provenance": "gold", "judge_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "protocol_hash": "65cea4ee79fd", "prof_total_s": 653.54, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 653.54, "prof_tok_in": 787, "prof_tok_out": 7168, "prof_llm_calls": 2}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-28T21:12:47.881406", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "amem", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_935e2cff-ae78-4218-b3f5-115589b19dae", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: In the year 2022, and before December, what does \"R\" stand for in the three core policies of the type of content that was violated in the public logs on the Legume Wikipedia page?", "augmented_prompt": "## Memories from earlier attempts (A-Mem)\n\n- Task: Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: In the year 2022, and before December, what does \"R\" stand for in the three core policies of the type of content that was violated in the public logs on the Legume Wikipedia page?\nAttempt: The three core Wikipedia content policies are NPOV, Verifiability, and No Original Research (NOR). The violated content type referenced in the Legume pa", "response": "The three core Wikipedia content policies are Neutral Point of View (NPOV), Verifiability (V), and No Original Research (NOR). In the acronym NOR, the “R” stands for “Research.”\n\nResearch", "expected": "research", "score": 1.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "1", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 445, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 1.0, "fb_mode": "gold", "code_rev": "56816631.fcf27e88", "critic_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "guarded", "score_provenance": "gold", "judge_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "protocol_hash": "65cea4ee79fd", "prof_total_s": 539.64, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 539.64, "prof_tok_in": 763, "prof_tok_out": 3902, "prof_llm_calls": 2}
