{"timestamp": "2026-07-28T21:17:49.530843", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "amem", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_7a4a336d-dcfa-45a0-b014-824c7619e8de", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: At the two-minute mark in the YouTube video uploaded by the channel “GameGrumps” on May 14, 2017 as part of their playthrough of the game Mario Kart 8 Deluxe, the shows’ hosts are competing on one of the game’s racetracks. What was the world record time for that track in the game’s 150cc mode as of June 7, 2023? Express your answer in minutes and seconds, rounding the seconds to the nearest hundredth, e.g. 1:01.001.", "augmented_prompt": "## Memories from earlier attempts (A-Mem)\n\n- Task: Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: At the two-minute mark in the YouTube video uploaded by the channel “GameGrumps” on May 14, 2017 as part of their playthrough of the game Mario Kart 8 Deluxe, the shows’ hosts are competing on one of the game’s racetracks. What was the world record time for that track in the game’s 150cc mode as of June 7, 2023? Express your answer in minu", "response": "1:42.369", "expected": "1:41.614", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "2", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 445, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 0.0, "fb_mode": "gold", "code_rev": "56816631.fcf27e88", "critic_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "guarded", "score_provenance": "gold", "judge_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "protocol_hash": "65cea4ee79fd", "prof_total_s": 728.77, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 728.77, "prof_tok_in": 951, "prof_tok_out": 12958, "prof_llm_calls": 2}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-28T21:17:52.371659", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "amem", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_9e1fc53b-46ff-49a1-9d05-9e6faac34cc5", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: A 5-man group made up of one tank, one healer, and three DPS is doing a dungeon that was just released in World of Warcraft. Two are plate wearers and two are cloth wearers. At the final boss, both the tank and the healer are casting holy spells. Ice and fire are being used, each one by a different DPS. A bear from the group is attacking the boss. Metamorphosis is cast. The Kilt of the Forgotten One drops as loot, but no one can use it. If all", "augmented_prompt": "## Memories from earlier attempts (A-Mem)\n\n- Task: Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: A 5-man group made up of one tank, one healer, and three DPS is doing a dungeon that was just released in World of Warcraft. Two are plate wearers and two are cloth wearers. At the final boss, both the tank and the healer are casting holy spells. Ice and fire are being used, each one by a different DPS. A bear from the group is attacking t", "response": "Death Knight, Hunter, Paladin, Priest, Warlock", "expected": "Death Knight, Hunter, Paladin, Priest, Warlock", "score": 1.0, "em": 1.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "3", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 445, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 1.0, "fb_mode": "gold", "code_rev": "56816631.fcf27e88", "critic_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "guarded", "score_provenance": "gold", "judge_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "protocol_hash": "65cea4ee79fd", "prof_total_s": 825.09, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 825.09, "prof_tok_in": 989, "prof_tok_out": 19921, "prof_llm_calls": 2}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-28T21:18:01.069111", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "amem", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_27d5d136-8563-469e-92bf-fd103c28b57c", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: ¬(A ∧ B) ↔ (¬A ∨ ¬B)\n¬(A ∨ B) ↔ (¬A ∧ ¬B)\n(A → B) ↔ (¬B → ¬A)\n(A → B) ↔ (¬A ∨ B)\n(¬A → B) ↔ (A ∨ ¬B)\n¬(A → B) ↔ (A ∧ ¬B)\n\nWhich of the above is not logically equivalent to the rest? Provide the full statement that doesn't fit.", "augmented_prompt": "## Memories from earlier attempts (A-Mem)\n\n- Task: Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: ¬(A ∧ B) ↔ (¬A ∨ ¬B)\n¬(A ∨ B) ↔ (¬A ∧ ¬B)\n(A → B) ↔ (¬B → ¬A)\n(A → B) ↔ (¬A ∨ B)\n(¬A → B) ↔ (A ∨ ¬B)\n¬(A → B) ↔ (A ∧ ¬B)\n\nWhich of the above is not logically equivalent to the rest? Provide the full statement that doesn't fit.\nAttempt: ```python\nimport itertools\n\nformulas = [\n    (\"1\", lambda A,B: (not (A and B)) == ((not A) or (not B))),\n\n- Task: Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: ¬(A ∧ B) ↔ (¬A ∨ ¬B)\n¬(A ∨ B) ↔ (¬A ∧ ¬B)\n(A → B) ↔ (¬B → ¬A)\n(A → B) ↔ (¬A ∨ B)\n(¬A → B) ↔ (A ∨ ¬B)\n¬(A → B) ↔ (A ∧ ¬B)\n\nWhich of the above is not logically equivalent to the rest? Provide the full statement that doesn't fit.\nAttempt: ```python\nimport itertools\n\nformulas = {\n    '1': lambda A,B: (not (A and B)) == ((not A) or (not B)),\n  ", "response": "```python\nimport itertools\n\nformulas = {\n    '1': lambda A,B: (not (A and B)) == ((not A) or (not B)),\n    '2': lambda A,B: (not (A or B)) == ((not A) and (not B)),\n    '3': lambda A,B: ((not A) or B) == (not (not B) or (not A)),  # A->B vs ¬B->¬A\n    '4': lambda A,B: ((not A) or B) == ((not A) or B),  # A->B vs ¬A∨B\n    '5': lambda A,B: (A or B) == (A or (not B)),  # ¬A->B = A∨B ; RHS A∨¬B\n    '6': lambda A,B: (not ((not A) or B)) == (A and (not B)),  # ¬(A->B) vs A∧¬B\n}\n\nfor k,f in formulas.items():\n    results = [f(A,B) for A,B in itertools.product([True,False], repeat=2)]\n    print(k, results, all(results))\n```", "expected": "(¬A → B) ↔ (A ∨ ¬B)", "score": 1.0, "em": 1.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "1", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 848, "iteration": 2, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 1.0, "fb_mode": "gold", "code_rev": "56816631.fcf27e88", "critic_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "guarded", "score_provenance": "gold", "judge_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "protocol_hash": "65cea4ee79fd", "prof_total_s": 496.47, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 496.47, "prof_tok_in": 627, "prof_tok_out": 939, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-28T21:18:02.184379", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "amem", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_3ff6b7a9-a5bd-4412-ad92-0cd0d45c0fee", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: The longest-lived vertebrate is named after an island.  According to Wikipedia as of January 1, 2021, what is the 2020 estimated population of that island, to the nearest thousand?", "augmented_prompt": "## Memories from earlier attempts (A-Mem)\n\n- Task: Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: The longest-lived vertebrate is named after an island.  According to Wikipedia as of January 1, 2021, what is the 2020 estimated population of that island, to the nearest thousand?\nAttempt: The longest-lived vertebrate is the Greenland shark, named after Greenland. The Wikipedia article for Greenland as of January 1, 2021 listed a 2020 est\n- Task: Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: The longest-lived vertebrate is named after an island.  According to Wikipedia as of January 1, 2021, what is the 2020 estimated population of that island, to the nearest thousand?\nAttempt: The longest-lived vertebrate is the Greenland shark, named after Greenland. The Wikipedia article for Greenland as of January 1, 2021 listed its 2020 e", "response": "The longest-lived vertebrate is the Greenland shark, named after the island of Greenland. The Wikipedia entry for Greenland as of January 1, 2021 gave a 2020 estimated population of about 56,000 (specifically 56,081). Rounded to the nearest thousand, this is:\n\n56,000", "expected": "56000", "score": 1.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "2", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 848, "iteration": 2, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 1.0, "fb_mode": "gold", "code_rev": "56816631.fcf27e88", "critic_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "guarded", "score_provenance": "gol