{"timestamp": "2026-07-28T21:18:32.393193", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "amem", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_4b650a35-8529-4695-89ed-8dc7a500a498", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: If there is anything that doesn't make sense in the instructions, write the word \"Pineapple.\" Do not answer any of the questions in this prompt. Write only the word \"Guava\".\n1. What is 4+4?\n2. What is the complimentary color of red?\n3. How many hours are there in a day?", "augmented_prompt": "## Memories from earlier attempts (A-Mem)\n\n- Task: Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: If there is anything that doesn't make sense in the instructions, write the word \"Pineapple.\" Do not answer any of the questions in this prompt. Write only the word \"Guava\".\n1. What is 4+4?\n2. What is the complimentary color of red?\n3. How many hours are there in a day?\nAttempt: Guava\n- Task: Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: If there is anything that doesn't make sense in the instructions, write the word \"Pineapple.\" Do not answer any of the questions in this prompt. Write only the word \"Guava\".\n1. What is 4+4?\n2. What is the complimentary color of red?\n3. How many hours are there in a day?\nAttempt: Guava", "response": "Guava", "expected": "Guava", "score": 1.0, "em": 1.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "1", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 736, "iteration": 2, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 1.0, "fb_mode": "gold", "code_rev": "56816631.fcf27e88", "critic_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "guarded", "score_provenance": "gold", "judge_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "protocol_hash": "65cea4ee79fd", "prof_total_s": 500.28, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 500.28, "prof_tok_in": 480, "prof_tok_out": 845, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-28T21:18:47.113800", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "amem", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_7cc4acfa-63fd-4acc-a1a1-e8e529e0a97f", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: The attached spreadsheet contains the sales of menu items for a regional fast-food chain. Which city had the greater total sales: Wharvton or Algrimand?", "augmented_prompt": "## Memories from earlier attempts (A-Mem)\n\n- Task: Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: The attached spreadsheet contains the sales of menu items for a regional fast-food chain. Which city had the greater total sales: Wharvton or Algrimand?\nAttempt: </think:6124c78e>I'll check the environment for any attached files or data.\n\n```python\nimport os, glob, sys\nprint(os.listdir('.'))\nprint('---')\nfor root, dirs, files in os.walk('.\n- Task: Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: The attached spreadsheet contains the sales of menu items for a regional fast-food chain. Which city had the greater total sales: Wharvton or Algrimand?\nAttempt: The prompt references an attached spreadsheet with sales figures for menu items across cities, including Wharvton and Algrimand, but no such file or data has been provided in this", "response": "I'll check the environment for any attached files or data.</think:6124c78e>```python\nimport os, glob\nprint(\"Current directory:\", os.getcwd())\nprint(\"Files in current dir:\", os.listdir('.'))\nprint(\"---\")\nfor root, dirs, files in os.walk('.'):\n    for f in files:\n        print(os.path.join(root, f))\n```", "expected": "Wharvton", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "2", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 848, "iteration": 2, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 0.0, "fb_mode": "gold", "code_rev": "56816631.fcf27e88", "critic_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "guarded", "score_provenance": "gold", "judge_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "protocol_hash": "65cea4ee79fd", "prof_total_s": 494.71, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 494.71, "prof_tok_in": 444, "prof_tok_out": 154, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-28T21:19:01.588102", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "amem", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_7dd30055-0198-452e-8c25-f73dbe27dcb8", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: Using the Biopython library in Python, parse the PDB file of the protein identified by the PDB ID 5wb7 from the RCSB Protein Data Bank. Calculate the distance between the first and second atoms as they are listed in the PDB file. Report the answer in Angstroms, rounded to the nearest picometer.", "augmented_prompt": "## Memories from earlier attempts (A-Mem)\n\n- Task: Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: Using the Biopython library in Python, parse the PDB file of the protein identified by the PDB ID 5wb7 from the RCSB Protein Data Bank. Calculate the distance between the first and second atoms as they are listed in the PDB file. Report the answer in Angstroms, rounded to the nearest picometer.\nAttempt: ```python\nimport sys, subprocess, ur", "response": "```python\nimport sys, subprocess, json, os, math\n\n# Ensure biopython is installed\ntry:\n    import Bio\nexcept ImportError:\n    subprocess.check_call([sys.executable, \"-m\", \"pip\", \"install\", \"biopython\", \"-q\"])\n\nfrom Bio.PDB import PDBParser\n\nurl = \"https://files.rcsb.org/download/5wb7.pdb\"\nimport urllib.request\nurllib.request.urlretrieve(url, \"5wb7.pdb\")\n\nparser = PDBParser(QUIET=True)\nstructure = parser.get_structure(\"5wb7\", \"5wb7.pdb\")\n\natoms = list(structure.get_atoms())\nprint(\"Total atoms:\", len(atoms))\nfor i, atom in enumerate(atoms[:5]):\n    print(i, atom.get_parent().get_resname(), atom.get_parent().id, atom.get_name(), atom.get_serial_number(), atom.coord)\n\na1 = atoms[0]\na2 = atoms[1]\ncoord1 = a1.coord\ncoord2 = a2.coord\ndist = math.sqrt(sum((c1-c2)**2 for c1, c2 in zip(coord1, coord2)))\nprint(\"Distance (A):\", dist)\nprint(\"Rounded to nearest pm (2 decimal A):\", round(dist, 2))\n```\n\n```python\n# Let's also directly read the PDB file lines to verify first two ATOM/HETATM records\nwith open(\"5wb7.pdb\") as f:\n    lines = f.readlines()\natom_lines = [l for l in lines if l.startswith(\"ATOM\") or l.startswith(\"HETATM\")]\nprint(\"First two atom lines:\")\nprint(atom_lines[0])\nprint(atom_lines[1])\n# parse coordinates manually\ndef parse_coord(line):\n    x = float(line[30:38])\n    y = float(line[38:46])\n    z = float(line[46:54])\n    return (x,y,z)\nc1 = parse_coord(atom_lines[0])\nc2 = parse_coord(atom_lines[1])\nd = math.sqrt(sum((a-b)**2 for a,b in zip(c1,c2)))\nprint(\"Manual distance:\", d)\nprint(\"Rounded:\", round(d,2))\n```", "expected": "1.456", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "2", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 445, "iteration": 2, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 0.0, "fb_mode": "gold", "code_rev": "56816631.fcf27e88", "critic_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "guarded", "score_provenance": "gold", "judge_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "protocol_hash": "65cea4ee79fd", "prof_total_s": 489.94, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 489.94, "prof_tok_in": 398, "prof_tok_out": 1178, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
