{"timestamp": "2026-07-28T21:19:53.194058", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "amem", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_b2c257e0-3ad7-4f05-b8e3-d9da973be36e", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: If this whole pint is made up of ice cream, how many percent above or below the US federal standards for butterfat content is it when using the standards as reported by Wikipedia in 2020? Answer as + or - a number rounded to one decimal place.", "augmented_prompt": "## Memories from earlier attempts (A-Mem)\n\n- Task: Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: If this whole pint is made up of ice cream, how many percent above or below the US federal standards for butterfat content is it when using the standards as reported by Wikipedia in 2020? Answer as + or - a number rounded to one decimal place.\nAttempt: I need to search for the specific context of this question, as it references \"this whole", "response": "The US federal standard for ice cream butterfat (per Wikipedia 2020) is 10%. Based on the typical pint nutrition label (e.g., Häagen‑Dazs: 13 g fat per ½‑cup serving, 4 servings, 106 g each), the whole pint has about 52 g butterfat in 424 g, i.e., ~12.3% butterfat. This is 2.3 percentage points above the 10% standard.\n\n+2.3", "expected": "+4.6", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "2", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 445, "iteration": 1, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 0.0, "fb_mode": "gold", "code_rev": "56816631.fcf27e88", "critic_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "guarded", "score_provenance": "gold", "judge_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "protocol_hash": "65cea4ee79fd", "prof_total_s": 653.88, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 653.88, "prof_tok_in": 777, "prof_tok_out": 11683, "prof_llm_calls": 2}
