{"timestamp": "2026-07-28T21:20:08.825406", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "amem", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_851e570a-e3de-4d84-bcfa-cc85578baa59", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: I thought we could try a fun word puzzle together :)\n\nI've got a Boggle board here:\n\nABRL\nEITE\nIONS\nFPEI\n\nI'd like to know the longest word that can be generated from the board. Please find the longest English language word that can be generated from this board. If more than one word of the same length exists at the maximum word length, please report the longest word that comes first, alphabetically. Oh, and I know that there might be differen", "augmented_prompt": "## Memories from earlier attempts (A-Mem)\n\n- Task: Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: I thought we could try a fun word puzzle together :)\n\nI've got a Boggle board here:\n\nABRL\nEITE\nIONS\nFPEI\n\nI'd like to know the longest word that can be generated from the board. Please find the longest English language word that can be generated from this board. If more than one word of the same length exists at the maximum word length, pl\n- Task: Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: I thought we could try a fun word puzzle together :)\n\nI've got a Boggle board here:\n\nABRL\nEITE\nIONS\nFPEI\n\nI'd like to know the longest word that can be generated from the board. Please find the longest English language word that can be generated from this board. If more than one word of the same length exists at the maximum word length, pl", "response": "```python\nimport urllib.request, sys, time\n\nurl = \"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/dwyl/english-words/master/words_alpha.txt\"\nprint(\"Downloading...\")\ntry:\n    with urllib.request.urlopen(url, timeout=30) as response:\n        data = response.read().decode('utf-8')\n    print(\"Downloaded length:\", len(data))\n    words = [w.strip().lower() for w in data.splitlines() if w.strip()]\n    print(\"Word count:\", len(words))\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print(\"Error:\", e)\n```", "expected": "Briniest", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "3", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 848, "iteration": 2, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 0.0, "fb_mode": "gold", "code_rev": "56816631.fcf27e88", "critic_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "guarded", "score_provenance": "gold", "judge_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "protocol_hash": "65cea4ee79fd", "prof_total_s": 510.62, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 510.62, "prof_tok_in": 557, "prof_tok_out": 670, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-28T21:20:22.612579", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "amem", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_3cef3a44-215e-4aed-8e3b-b1e3f08063b7", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: I'm making a grocery list for my mom, but she's a professor of botany and she's a real stickler when it comes to categorizing things. I need to add different foods to different categories on the grocery list, but if I make a mistake, she won't buy anything inserted in the wrong category. Here's the list I have so far:\n\nmilk, eggs, flour, whole bean coffee, Oreos, sweet potatoes, fresh basil, plums, green beans, rice, corn, bell pepper, whole a", "augmented_prompt": "## Memories from earlier attempts (A-Mem)\n\n- Task: Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: I'm making a grocery list for my mom, but she's a professor of botany and she's a real stickler when it comes to categorizing things. I need to add different foods to different categories on the grocery list, but if I make a mistake, she won't buy anything inserted in the wrong category. Here's the list I have so far:\n\nmilk, eggs, flour, w\n- Task: Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: I'm making a grocery list for my mom, but she's a professor of botany and she's a real stickler when it comes to categorizing things. I need to add different foods to different categories on the grocery list, but if I make a mistake, she won't buy anything inserted in the wrong category. Here's the list I have so far:\n\nmilk, eggs, flour, w", "response": "To classify botanically, we exclude all items that are fruits (including grains, nuts, legumes, and berries) and non-plant/animal/processed foods. From the list, the only non-fruit plant parts are: sweet potatoes (storage root), fresh basil (leaves), broccoli (flower buds), celery (petioles), and lettuce (leaves). Alphabetizing these gives:\n\nbroccoli, celery, fresh basil, lettuce, sweet potatoes", "expected": "broccoli, celery, fresh basil, lettuce, sweet potatoes", "score": 1.0, "em": 1.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "1", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 848, "iteration": 2, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 1.0, "fb_mode": "gold", "code_rev": "56816631.fcf27e88", "critic_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "guarded", "score_provenance": "gold", "judge_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "protocol_hash": "65cea4ee79fd", "prof_total_s": 552.71, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 552.71, "prof_tok_in": 1335, "prof_tok_out": 4106, "prof_llm_calls": 2}
