{"timestamp": "2026-07-28T21:20:54.175832", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "amem", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_a3fbeb63-0e8c-4a11-bff6-0e3b484c3e9c", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: How many slides in this PowerPoint presentation mention crustaceans?", "augmented_prompt": "## Memories from earlier attempts (A-Mem)\n\n- Task: Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: How many slides in this PowerPoint presentation mention crustaceans?\nAttempt: ```python\nimport os, glob, sys\n\n# list current directory and common locations\nfor root in ['.', '/', '/home', '/tmp', '/mnt', '/data']:\n    try:\n        print(root, os.listdir(root)[:50])\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(root, 'err', e)\n\nprint('--- pptx s\n- Task: Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: How many slides in this PowerPoint presentation mention crustaceans?\nAttempt: Since no PowerPoint file or content was provided in this environment and no tools are available to access any external presentation, there are no slides to examine. Consequently, the number of slides that mention crustaceans is zero.\n\n0", "response": "```python\nimport os, glob\n\npaths = []\nfor root in ['.', '/home', '/tmp', '/mnt', '/data', '/workspace', '/app']:\n    try:\n        for dirpath, dirnames, filenames in os.walk(root):\n            for f in filenames:\n                if f.lower().endswith(('.pptx', '.ppt', '.odp')):\n                    paths.append(os.path.join(dirpath, f))\n    except Exception as e:\n        pass\n\nprint('found:', paths[:100])\n```", "expected": "4", "score": 0.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "1", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 821, "iteration": 2, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 0.0, "fb_mode": "gold", "code_rev": "56816631.fcf27e88", "critic_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "guarded", "score_provenance": "gold", "judge_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "protocol_hash": "65cea4ee79fd", "prof_total_s": 498.71, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 498.71, "prof_tok_in": 409, "prof_tok_out": 529, "prof_llm_calls": 1}
{"timestamp": "2026-07-28T21:20:57.064675", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "amem", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_11af4e1a-5f45-467d-9aeb-46f4bb0bf034", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: How many more blocks (also denoted as layers) in BERT base encoder than the encoder from the architecture proposed in Attention is All You Need?", "augmented_prompt": "## Memories from earlier attempts (A-Mem)\n\n- Task: Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: How many more blocks (also denoted as layers) in BERT base encoder than the encoder from the architecture proposed in Attention is All You Need?\nAttempt: BERT-base encoder uses 12 layers. The encoder in \"Attention is All You Need\" uses N=6 layers. The difference is 12 - 6 = 6.\n\n6\n- Task: Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: How many more blocks (also denoted as layers) in BERT base encoder than the encoder from the architecture proposed in Attention is All You Need?\nAttempt: BERT-base uses 12 transformer encoder layers (blocks). The encoder in the original Transformer architecture from \"Attention is All You Need\" uses N = 6 layers. The difference is 12 − 6 = ", "response": "BERT-base uses a transformer encoder with 12 layers (blocks). The encoder architecture described in \"Attention is All You Need\" (the base Transformer) uses N = 6 layers. The difference is 12 − 6 = 6.\n\n6", "expected": "6", "score": 1.0, "em": 0.0, "method": "exact_match", "execution_mode": "default", "error": "", "category": "", "level": "1", "patch_injected": true, "aug_len": 787, "iteration": 2, "iter_total": 3, "mutated": false, "fb_score": 1.0, "fb_mode": "gold", "code_rev": "56816631.fcf27e88", "critic_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "metadata_author": "critic", "c_meta": false, "c_policy": "guarded", "score_provenance": "gold", "judge_model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "protocol_hash": "65cea4ee79fd", "prof_total_s": 503.63, "prof_embed_s": 0.0, "prof_docker_s": 0.0, "prof_llm_io_s": 503.63,