{"timestamp": "2026-07-28T21:24:39.392243", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "amem", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_0a3cd321-3e76-4622-911b-0fda2e5d6b1a", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: According to the World Bank, which countries had gross savings of over 35% of GDP for every year in the period 2001-2010? Give your answer as a comma-separated list of countries in alphabetical order. Use the countries most common names in english when answering.", "augmented_prompt": "## Memories from earlier attempts (A-Mem)\n\n- Task: Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: According to the World Bank, which countries had gross savings of over 35% of GDP for every year in the period 2001-2010? Give your answer as a comma-separated list of countries in alphabetical order. Use the countries most common names in english when answering.\nAttempt: ```python\nimport urllib.request, json\n\nindicator = \"NY.GNS.ICT.ZS\"\nu\n- Task: Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: According to the World Bank, which countries had gross savings of over 35% of GDP for every year in the period 2001-2010? Give your answer as a comma-separated list of countries in alphabetical order. Use the countries most common names in english when answering.\nAttempt: ```python\nimport urllib.request, json, time\n\nindicator = \"NY.GNS.ICT", "response": "```python\nimport urllib.request, json\n\nindicator = \"NY.GNS.ICT.ZS\"\nurl = f\"https://api.worldbank.org/v2/country/all/indicator/{indicator}?date=2001:2010&format=json&per_page=20000\"\nwith urllib.request.urlopen(url) as r:\n    data = json.load(r)\n# data[0] metadata, data[1] list\nprint(\"pages:\", data[0]['pages'], \"per_page:\", data[0]['per_page'], \"total:\", data[0]['total'])\nprint(len(data[1]))\n# inspect one\nprint(data[1][0])\n```\n\n```python\n# Build dict: country -> {year: value}\nfrom collections import defaultdict\ncountries = {}\nfor row in data[1]:\n    c = row['country']['value']\n    iso = row['countryiso3code']\n    year = row['date']\n    val = row['value']\n    if val is None:\n        continue\n    countries.setdefault(c, {})[int(year)] = val\n\n# years required\nreq_years = list(range(2001,2011))\nqualifying = []\nfor c, vals in countries.items():\n    if all((y in vals) and (vals[y] > 35) for y in req_years):\n        qualifying.append(c)\nprint(\"Number qualifying:\", len(qualifying))\nprint(sorted(qualifying))\n```\n\n```python\n# Let's also check if any country has missing years but maybe World Bank uses different aggregation? We'll list those with all years present and >35.\n# Print with values for sanity\nfor c in sorted(qualifying):\n    print(c, [countries[c][y] for y in req_years])\n```\n\n```python\n# Need common English names. Let's see the exact names returned.\nfor c in sorted(qualifying):\n    print(repr(c))\n```\n\n```python\n# Let's also fetch country metadata to get iso and maybe region? Not needed.\n# But we should verify by checking World Bank data via another source? Could also download CSV.\n# Let's check if there are any countries with name variants like \"Korea, Rep.\" etc in list.\nprint(sorted(qualifying))\n```\n\n```python\n# Let's also consider that some countries might be aggregates like \"World\", \"Sub-Saharan Africa\" etc. We should exclude aggregate regions.\n# World Bank API includes region aggregates with iso codes like 'WLD','ARB','CSS','CEB','EAR','EAS','ECS','ECA','EMU','EUU','FCS','HIC','HPC','IBD','IBT','IDB','IDX','LAC','LCN','LDC','LMY','LTE','LIC','LMC','MEA','MIC','MNA','NAC','OED','OSS','PSS','PST','PRE','SST','SAS','SSF','SSA','STN','TLA','TMN','TSA','TSS','UMC','WLD'\n# Let's fetch list of aggregates? We'll just filter out those with numeric iso? Actually countryiso3code for aggregates may be empty or region code.\n# Let's inspect iso for qualifying.\nfor c in sorted(qualifying):\n    # find iso from data\n    pass\n# Let's rebuild with iso.\ncountries_iso = {}\nfor row in data[1]:\n    c = row['country']['value']\n    iso = row['countryiso3code']\n    year = row['date']\n    val = row['value']\n    if val is None:\n        continue\n    countries_iso.setdefault(c, (iso, {}))[1][int(year)] = val\n\nqual_iso = []\nfor c, (iso, vals) in countries_iso.items():\n    if all((y in vals) and (vals[y] > 35) for y in req_years):\n        qual_iso.append((c, iso))\nfor c, iso in sorted(qual_iso):\n    print(iso, c)\n```\n\n```python\n# Let's get list of aggregate iso codes from World Bank.\nagg_url = \"https://api.worldbank.org/v2/country?format=json&per_page=20000\"\nwith urllib.request.urlopen(agg_url) as r:\n    cdata = json.load(r)\n# cdata[1] list of countries/aggregates with 'region' maybe 'Aggregates'\naggs = [c['iso3Code'] for c in cdata[1] if c.get('region') and c['region']['value'] == 'Aggregates']\nprint(\"Aggregate codes count:\", len(aggs))\nprint(aggs[:20])\n```\n\n```python\n# Filter qualifying to exclude aggregates\nqual_clean = []\nfor c, iso in qual_iso:\n    if iso in aggs:\n        print(\"Excluding aggregate:\", c, iso)\n    else:\n        qual_clean.append(c)\nprint(\"Clean qualifying:\", len(qual_clean))\nprint(sorted(qual_clean))\n```\n\n```python\n# Let's double-check by fetching the indicator page maybe there is a CSV with all data. But API is fine.\n# However, need to ensure we didn't miss countries due to pagination. per_page=20000, total maybe ~? Let's check total.\nprint(data[0]['total'])\n```\n\n```python\n# Let's also verify that the API returns all countries for all years. If total > per_page, need pages. But per_page=20000 likely enough (indicator * countries * years ~ 300*10=3000). So fine.\n# Now map to common English names.\n# Let's list the raw names we have:\nraw_names = sorted(qual_clean)\nprint(raw_names)\n```\n\n```python\n# We'll manually map based on known World Bank naming:\n# Possible names from WB: \n# \"Brunei Darussalam\" -> Brunei\n# \"Congo, Dem. Rep.\" -> DR Congo? common: Democratic Republic of the Congo\n# \"Congo, Rep.\" -> Republic of the Congo\n# \"Egypt, Arab Rep.\" -> Egypt\n# \"Gambia, The\" -> Gambia\n# \"Hong Kong SAR, China\" -> Hong Kong? (not a country but often listed; question says countries; but WB includes economies. Should we include? It says countries. Hong Kong is not a country. Might exclude? Need decide. The question: \"which countries had gross savings...\" According to World Bank, they often refer to economies. But they say countries. We'll include only sovereign states? Hmm.\n# \"Iran, Islamic Rep.\" -> Iran\n# \"Korea, Rep.\" -> South Korea\n# \"Kuwait\"\n# \"Lao PDR\" -> Laos\n# \"Macao SAR, China\" -> Macau? not country.\n# \"Mongolia\"\n# \"Myanmar\" (maybe \"Myanmar\"?)\n# \"Niger\"? maybe not.\n# \"Norway\"? maybe.\n# \"Oman\"\n# \"Qatar\"\n# \"Saudi Arabia\"\n# \"Singapore\"\n# \"Syrian Arab Republic\" -> Syria\n# \"Timor-Leste\"\n# \"Turkmenistan\"\n# \"United Arab Emirates\"\n# \"Uzbekistan\"? maybe.\n# \"Venezuela, RB\" -> Venezuela\n# \"Vietnam\"\n# \"Yemen, Rep.\" -> Yemen\n# \"Zambia\"? maybe not.\n# \"Zimbabwe\"? maybe not.\n# \"China\"? maybe.\n# \"Botswana\"? maybe.\n# \"Equatorial Guinea\"? maybe.\n# \"Gabon\"? maybe.\n# \"Kazakhstan\"? maybe.\n# \"Russia\"? maybe \"Russian Federation\" -> Russia.\n# \"Suriname\"? maybe.\n# \"Libya\"? maybe \"Libya\".\n# \"Algeria\"? maybe.\n# \"Iraq\"? maybe.\n# \"Kuwait\" etc.\n# Let's see actual raw list from output. We need to run print.\n```\n\n```python\n# Let's output raw names exactly as sorted.\nfor n in raw_names:\n    print(n)\n```\n\n```python\n# We need to see the output. Let's run a cell that prints them line by line.\n```\n\n```python\n# Actually we haven't seen output because previous code didn't print? It did but not shown? Let's re-run with explicit print.\nprint(\"\\n\".join(raw_names))\n```\n\n```python\n# Let's also compute again to be safe with exact condition >35 (strictly greater). Some might be exactly 35? We need over 35, so >35.\n# Let's also output values for each