{"timestamp": "2026-07-28T21:28:36.081061", "benchmark": "gaia", "group": "amem", "phase": "test", "task_id": "gaia_1f975693-876d-457b-a649-393859e79bf3", "task_desc": "Answer the following question accurately.\n\nQuestion: Hi, I was out sick from my classes on Friday, so I'm trying to figure out what I need to study for my Calculus mid-term next week. My friend from class sent me an audio recording of Professor Willowbrook giving out the recommended reading for the test, but my headphones are broken :(\n\nCould you please listen to the recording for me and tell me the page numbers I'm supposed to go over? I've attached a file called Homework.mp3 that has the recor", "augmented_prompt": "", "response": "I'll help you extract the page numbers from the audio recording. Let me first check the file and then process it.\n\nTool call list:\n1. Tool: `execute_code`\n   - `code` = `import os\nimport glob\n\n# Check for the audio file\nfiles = glob.glob(\"*.mp3\")\nprint(\"MP3 files found:\", files)\n\n# Also check current directory contents\nfor f in os.listdir('.'):\n    if os.path.isfile(f):\n        print(f, os.path.getsize(f))`\n\n1. Tool: `execute_code`\n   - `code` = `# Try to check if speech recognition libraries are available\ntry:\n    import speech_recognition as sr\n    print(\"speech_recognition available\")\nexcept ImportError as e:\n    print(\"speech_recognition not available:\", e)\n\ntry:\n    import whisper\n    print(\"whisper available\")\nexcept ImportError as e:\n    print(\"whisper not available:\", e)\n\ntry:\n    import torch\n    print(\"torch available\")\nexcept ImportError as e:\n    print(\"torch not available:\", e)`\n\n1. Tool: `execute_code`\n   - `code` = `# Check for audio processing libraries\ntry:\n    import pydub\n    print(\"pydub available\")\nexcept ImportError as e:\n    print(\"pydub not available:\", e)\n\ntry:\n    import librosa\n    print(\"librosa available\")\nexcept ImportError as e:\n    print(\"librosa not available:\", e)\n\ntry:\n    import soundfile\n    print(\"soundfile available\")\nexcept ImportError as e:\n    print(\"soundfile not available:\", e)`\n\n1. Tool: `execute_code`\n   - `code` = `# Check for ffmpeg\nimport shutil\nprint(\"ffmpeg:\", shutil.which(\"ffmpeg\"))\nprint(\"ffprobe:\", shutil.which(\"ffprobe\"))`\n\n1. Tool: `execute_code`\n   - `code` = `# Check internet access for possible API-based transcription\nimport urllib.request\ntry:\n    urllib.request.urlopen(\"https://www.google.com\", timeout=5)\n    print(\"Internet available\")\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print(\"No internet:\", e)`\n\n1. Tool: `execute_code`\n   - `code` = `# Check for other possible transcription tools\nimport subprocess\ntools = [\"sox\", \"ffmpeg\", \"vosk\", \"kaldi\"]\nfor t in tools:\n    print(t, shutil.which(t))`\n\n1. Tool: `execute_code`\n   - `code` = `# Let's see if we can install anything\nimport sys\nprint(sys.version)\nprint(sys.executable)`\n\n1. Tool: `execute_code`\n   - `code` = `# Check pip packages related to audio/ML\nimport pkgutil\nmods = [m.name for m in pkgutil.iter_modules()]\naudio_mods = [m for m in mods if any(k in m.lower() for k in ['speech','audio','whisper','vosk','asr','transcrib','recogn'])]\nprint(\"Audio/ASR related modules:\", audio_mods)`\n\n1. Tool: `execute_code`\n   - `code` = `# Let's try to read the mp3 file header to understand it\nwith open('Homework.mp3', 'rb') as f:\n    header = f.read(100)\nprint(header[:20])\nprint(len(header))`\n\n1. Tool: `execute_code`\n   - `code` = `# Try to use pydub to load and convert\ntry:\n    from pydub import AudioSegment\n    audio = AudioSegment.from_mp3(\"Homework.mp3\")\n    print(\"Duration:\", audio.duration_seconds)\n    print(\"Channels:\", audio.channels)\n    print(\"Frame rate:\", audio.frame_rate)\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print(\"Error:\", e)`\n\n1. Tool: `execute_code`\n   - `code` = `# Try to install whisper or use existing tools\n# First check if we can pip install\nimport subprocess\nresult = subprocess.run([sys.executable, \"-m\", \"pip\", \"list\"], capture_output=True, text=True)\nprint(result.stdout[:2000])`\n\n1. Tool: `execute_code`\n   - `code` = `# Let's try to install openai-whisper or faster-whisper\nimport subprocess\ntry:\n    result = subprocess.run([sys.executable, \"-m\", \"pip\", \"install\", \"faster-whisper\"], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=120)\n    print(\"STDOUT:\", result.stdout[-1000:])\n    print(\"STDERR:\", result.stderr[-1000:])\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print(\"Install failed:\", e)`\n\n1. Tool: `execute_code`\n   - `code` = `# Check if faster-whisper installed\ntry:\n    from faster_whisper import WhisperModel\n    print(\"faster_whisper available\")\nexcept ImportError as e:\n    print(\"faster_whisper not available:\", e)`\n\n1. Tool: `execute_code`\n   - `code` = `# Try to install openai-whisper as alternative\nimport subprocess\ntry:\n    result = subprocess.run([sys.executable, \"-m\", \"pip\", \"install\", \"openai-whisper\"], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=180)\n    print(\"STDOUT:\", result.stdout[-1000:])\n    print(\"STDERR:\", result.stderr[-1000:])\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print(\"Install failed:\", e)`\n\n1. Tool: `execute_code`\n   - `code` = `# Check if whisper installed\ntry:\n    import whisper\n    print(\"whisper available\")\nexcept ImportError as e:\n    print(\"whisper not available:\", e)`\n\n1. Tool: `execute_code`\n   - `code` = `# Try vosk as alternative - lightweight\nimport subprocess\ntry:\n    result = subprocess.run([sys.executable, \"-m\", \"pip\", \"install\", \"vosk\"], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=120)\n    print(\"STDOUT:\", result.stdout[-500:])\n    print(\"STDERR:\", result.stderr[-500:])\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print(\"Install failed:\", e)`\n\n1. Tool: `execute_code`\n   - `code` = `# Check vosk\ntry:\n    from vosk import Model, KaldiRecognizer\n    print(\"vosk available\")\nexcept ImportError as e:\n    print(\"vosk not available:\", e)`\n\n1. Tool: `execute_code`\n   - `code` = `# Let's try to use speech_recognition with sphinx (offline) if available\ntry:\n    import speech_recognition as sr\n    r = sr.Recognizer()\n    print(\"Recognizer created\")\n    # Check if pocketsphinx is available\n    try:\n        print(sr.Recognizer().recognize_sphinx)\n        print(\"sphinx available\")\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(\"sphinx not available:\", e)\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print(\"speech_recognition issue:\", e)`\n\n1. Tool: `execute_code`\n   - `code` = `# Let's try to install pocketsphinx\nimport subprocess\ntry:\n    result = subprocess.run([sys.executable, \"-m\", \"pip\", \"install\", \"pocketsphinx\"], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=120)\n    print(\"STDOUT:\", result.stdout[-500:])\n    print(\"STDERR:\", result.stderr[-500:])\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print(\"Install failed:\", e)`\n\n1. Tool: `execute_code`\n   - `code` = `# Check pocketsphinx\ntry:\n    import pocketsphinx\n    print(\"pocketsphinx available\")\nexcept ImportError as e:\n    print(\"pocketsphinx not available:\", e)`\n\n1. Tool: `execute_code`\n   - `code` = `# Let's try to do the actual transcription with whatever we have\n# First, let's convert mp3 to wav using pydub if available\ntry:\n    from pydub import AudioSegment\n    sound = AudioSegment.from_mp3(\"Homework.mp3\")\n    sound.export(\"audio.wav\", format=\"wav\")\n    print(\"Converted to wav\")\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print(\"Conversion error:\", e)`\n\n1. Tool: `execute_code`\n   - `code` = `# Try transcription with whisper if available\ntry:\n    import whisper\n    model = whisper.load_model(\"base\")\n    result = model.transcribe(\"Homework.mp3\")\n    print(\"TRANSCRIPTION:\")\n    print(result[\"text\"])\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print(\"Whisper error:\", e)`\n\n1. Tool: `execute_code`\n   - `code` = `# Try faster-whisper\ntry:\n    from faster_whisper import WhisperModel\n    model = WhisperModel(\"base\", device=\"cpu\")\n    segments, info = model.transcribe(\"Homework.mp3\")\n    text = \"\"\n    for segment in segments:\n        text += segment.text\n    print(\"TRANSCRIPTION:\")\n    print(text)\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print(\"Faster-whisper error:\", e)`\n\n1. Tool: `execute_code`\n   - `code` = `# Try vosk\nimport os\ntry:\n    from vosk import Model, KaldiRecognizer\n    import wave\n    # Need model - check if we can download\n    if not os.path.exists(\"vosk-model\"):\n        print(\"Need to download vosk model\")\n    else:\n        wf = wave.open(\"audio.wav\", \"rb\")\n        model = Model(\"vosk-model\")\n        rec = KaldiRecognizer(model, wf.getframerate())\n        text = \"\"\n        while True:\n            data = wf.readframes(4000)\n            if len(data) == 0:\n                break\n            if rec.AcceptWaveform(data):\n                text += rec.Result()\n        text += rec.FinalResult()\n        print(\"TRANSCRIPTION:\", text)\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print(\"Vosk error:\", e)`\n\n1. Tool: `execute_code`\n   - `code` = `# Let's try to download a small vosk model\nimport subprocess\ntry:\n    # Small English model\n    url = \"https://alphacephei.com/vosk/models/vosk-model-small-en-us-0.15.zip\"\n    result = subprocess.run([\"wget\", url, \"-O\", \"vosk-model.zip\"], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=120)\n    print(\"Download stdout:\", result.stdout[-300:])\n    print(\"Download stderr:\", result.stderr[-300:])\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print(\"Download failed:\", e)`\n\n1. Tool: `execute_code`\n   - `code` = `# Check if wget worked\nimport os\nprint(\"vosk-model.zip exists:\", os.path.exists(\"vosk-model.zip\"))\nif os.path.exists(\"vosk-model.zip\"):\n    print(\"Size:\", os.path.getsize(\"vosk-model.zip\"))`\n\n1. Tool: `execute_code`\n   - `code` = `# Unzip the model\nimport subprocess\ntry:\n    result = subprocess.run([\"unzip\", \"vosk-model.zip\"], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=60)\n    print(\"Unzip st